00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:44,480
Find them and get rid of them this
instant, Meow.

262
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:45,740
Yes, sir, Meow.

263
00:13:47,245 --> 00:13:49,660
A human in my stronghold?

264
00:13:49,940 --> 00:13:52,380
It's been seven years since the last time.

265
00:13:52,780 --> 00:13:55,680
No, it couldn't be, Meow.

266
00:14:11,120 --> 00:14:14,980
If I can't go through the front gate,
I'll just sneak in from the side.

267
00:14:15,140 --> 00:14:16,880
I am a ninja, after all.

268
00:14:31,209 --> 00:14:33,440
The best place to get information is a
bar.

269
00:14:56,940 --> 00:14:59,500
Your catnip drink, miss, Meow.

270
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:03,140
Thanks, but I didn't actually order
anything yet, Meow.

271
00:15:03,820 --> 00:15:05,440
Compliments to that customer.

272
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:09,840
Hello.

273
00:15:10,220 --> 00:15:11,900
May I come and join you, Meow?

274
00:15:12,309 --> 00:15:13,309
Oh, sure.

275
00:15:21,540 --> 00:15:24,120
Well, always nice to meet someone new.

276
00:15:24,121 --> 00:15:25,580
How about a little treat?

277
00:15:30,079 --> 00:15:32,180
You simply must try this, Meow.

278
00:15:35,580 --> 00:15:36,540
Excuse me.

279
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:39,200
By any chance, do you happen to know a cat
named Nekomata?

280
00:15:39,540 --> 00:15:40,320
Boss, yeah.

281
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:42,020
He always stays in the main tower.

282
00:15:42,380 --> 00:15:44,080
Oh, thank you very much.

283
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:45,800
Have this if you want, Meow.

284
00:15:46,160 --> 00:15:46,640
Really?

285
00:15:46,641 --> 00:15:47,641
Really?

286
00:16:02,220 --> 00:16:03,700
Rigged plastic bottles?

287
00:16:03,940 --> 00:16:06,900
These are supposed to be used against
cats, not by them!

288
00:16:10,220 --> 00:16:12,440
Boss is in the main tower.

289
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:13,600
There.

290
00:16:19,310 --> 00:16:21,290
We know and we're beaten.

291
00:16:21,470 --> 00:16:22,130
We surrender.

292
00:16:22,490 --> 00:16:22,870
Meow.

293
00:16:22,871 --> 00:16:23,871
Meow.

294
00:16:33,220 --> 00:16:36,200
So, you managed to make it all the way
here.

295
00:16:36,980 --> 00:16:39,020
Who are you, Meow?

296
00:16:40,220 --> 00:16:41,900
You're the one they call Nekomata.

297
00:16:42,360 --> 00:16:44,980
It'll be easier if you volunteer your paw
print.

298
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:47,700
Otherwise, it's going to get painful.

299
00:16:48,840 --> 00:16:51,014
I'm impressed that you
have the guts to stand

300
00:16:51,015 --> 00:16:53,821
before me and make a
threat like that, Meow.

301
00:16:54,720 --> 00:16:55,720
However...

302
00:17:04,859 --> 00:17:05,859
What is this?

303
00:17:14,939 --> 00:17:16,339
Who are you?

304
00:17:18,020 --> 00:17:19,020
Meow!

305
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:25,920
Meow!

306
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:26,960
Meow!

307
00:17:27,079 --> 00:17:27,260
Meow!

308
00:17:27,261 --> 00:17:27,660
Meow!

309
00:17:28,119 --> 00:17:29,120
Meow!

310
00:17:49,370 --> 00:17:55,270
Sounds like there is a story behind this.

311
00:17:55,271 --> 00:17:56,271
Huh?

312
00:17:59,270 --> 00:18:00,710
Since the first day, Nekomata has killed
me.

313
00:18:00,711 --> 00:18:01,410
I want to be a part of the story.

314
00:18:01,430 --> 00:18:01,510
You're my brother.

315
00:18:02,310 --> 00:18:03,310
I don't think I can help.

316
00:18:04,430 --> 00:18:05,670
A first-class house.

317
00:18:05,830 --> 00:18:06,570
Yes, sir.

318
00:18:06,571 --> 00:18:06,590
You are not alone.

319
00:18:06,591 --> 00:18:07,591
I am.

320
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,400
BEGONE!

321
00:18:35,800 --> 00:18:38,080
Mission Accomplished.

322
00:18:42,600 --> 00:18:46,920
I'd say you certainly drew an unlucky hand
of cards that time, Nekomata.

323
00:18:48,260 --> 00:18:54,141
Nah, I wanted to have a go with Itachi's
brother, so I could see what he was made of.

324
00:18:54,600 --> 00:18:58,160
Besides, I couldn't refuse a request from
Itachi, now could I?

325
00:19:01,220 --> 00:19:02,220
You mewnster!

326
00:19:03,360 --> 00:19:06,360
In time, my kid brother will come to see
you.

327
00:19:06,660 --> 00:19:09,940
And when he does, I want you to fight him
with all your might.

328
00:19:10,450 --> 00:19:13,340
He probably won't have the strength to
defeat you yet.

329
00:19:14,220 --> 00:19:16,040
Then why do it?

330
00:19:16,360 --> 00:19:20,040
Because growth occurs when one is pushed
beyond his limits.

331
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:23,320
That knowledge is a vital part of
training.

332
00:19:24,760 --> 00:19:27,537
I hate to admit it,
but when he faced me,

333
00:19:27,538 --> 00:19:31,561
Sasuke passed Itachi's
test with flying colors.

334
00:19:31,800 --> 00:19:33,620
Indeed, I agree with you.

335
00:19:34,140 --> 00:19:36,160
But it's so unfortunate.

336
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:39,840
Those two boys were so close when they
were young.

337
00:19:50,300 --> 00:19:50,577
I don't want to see
them fight each other,

338
00:19:50,577 --> 00:19:50,800
but I don't want to see
them fight each other.

339
00:19:50,801 --> 00:19:51,801
That's it!

340
00:19:52,060 --> 00:19:54,440
Nothing's going to stop me from seeing
that face!

341
00:19:54,870 --> 00:19:55,660
Yeah, but how?

342
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:56,800
You got any ideas?

343
00:19:57,199 --> 00:19:58,199
Don't you worry.

344
00:19:58,514 --> 00:20:01,000
We'll see it one way or another!

345
00:20:01,300 --> 00:20:03,600
I'm asking you how, you stupid little
troll!

346
00:20:04,900 --> 00:20:08,400
All right, smarty pants, how do you
propose we do it?

347
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:09,760
Well, we...

348
00:20:10,059 --> 00:20:12,100
We'll just have to tail him around for the
day.

349
00:20:12,639 --> 00:20:14,039
He'll take off the mask eventually.

350
00:20:14,664 --> 00:20:16,980
Oh, Sasuke, I swear you are so smart!

351
00:20:17,340 --> 00:20:17,860
Oh, whatever.

352
00:20:18,020 --> 00:20:18,960
Good plan, Captain.

353
00:20:18,961 --> 00:20:19,560
Captain Obvious!

354
00:20:19,600 --> 00:20:20,940
I'm sorry, what was that?

355
00:20:21,659 --> 00:20:22,780
Uh, never mind.

356
00:20:32,720 --> 00:20:35,920
What in the world is Kakashi-sensei doing?

357
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:37,520
It's so disappointing.

358
00:20:38,920 --> 00:20:39,920
He's onto us.

359
00:20:40,354 --> 00:20:42,500
Naruto, you idiot, you blew our cover!

360
00:20:43,009 --> 00:20:44,460
Why the heck is it my fault?

361
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:47,700
Wait.

362
00:20:47,701 --> 00:20:50,600
My favorite book is going to be a movie?

363
00:20:51,940 --> 00:20:53,880
I better order tickets in advance!

364
00:20:54,380 --> 00:20:56,040
Hey, he's on the move!

365
00:20:56,300 --> 00:20:57,760
Let's go before we lose him.

366
00:20:57,980 --> 00:20:58,980
Yeah, right!

367
00:21:03,040 --> 00:21:04,040
He's gone!

368
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:06,640
Oh, great, he got away.

369
00:21:07,020 --> 00:21:08,080
Are you kidding?

370
00:21:08,320 --> 00:21:09,720
Where did he vanish off to?

371
00:21:10,020 --> 00:21:12,340
Hey, what are you three doing?

372
00:21:12,880 --> 00:21:14,820
Do you guys need me for something?

373
00:21:15,380 --> 00:21:16,820
No, not really!

374
00:21:18,960 --> 00:21:19,960
Hmm...

375
00:21:24,020 --> 00:21:26,416
This thing has the
creepiest eyes, like it's always

376
00:21:26,417 --> 00:21:28,581
thinking about trying
to eat me or something.

377
00:21:29,079 --> 00:21:30,320
Oh, don't be ridiculous.

378
00:21:30,620 --> 00:21:31,660
I think it's kind of cute.

379
00:21:32,240 --> 00:21:35,520
Anyway, you're the one who drew the short
stick, so you're just going to have to

380
00:21:35,521 --> 00:21:37,480
take care of it until we get back to the
village.

381
00:21:39,280 --> 00:21:42,520
If it's any consolation, you two make
quite a cute couple.

382
00:21:44,660 --> 00:21:46,960
How can you say this thing is cute?

383
00:21:47,580 --> 00:21:48,100
Ow!

384
00:21:48,101 --> 00:21:48,540
Ow!

385
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:48,960
Ow!

386
00:21:49,120 --> 00:21:50,200
Quick, cut it out!

387
00:21:50,320 --> 00:21:50,820
Come on!

388
00:21:51,320 --> 00:21:52,980
First it was a stray cat.

389
00:21:53,300 --> 00:21:55,080
Then a stray dog and a pig.

390
00:21:55,240 --> 00:21:56,920
Now it's a stray ostrich.

391
00:21:57,660 --> 00:22:00,542
Well, we may be going up
in size, but I don't see how

392
00:22:00,543 --> 00:22:03,040
these silly missions are
supposed to improve our skills.

393
00:22:04,440 --> 00:22:05,440
Missions, huh?

394
00:22:05,820 --> 00:22:08,940
The purpose of these missions isn't to
improve your skills.

395
00:22:09,280 --> 00:22:11,140
You're not doing this for training.

396
00:22:16,074 --> 00:22:19,080
Although I understand why you may be
getting impatient.

397
00:22:20,800 --> 00:22:22,140
Hey, here's an idea.

398
00:22:22,340 --> 00:22:25,180
Why don't you improve your skills by
taking care of this ostrich?

399
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:26,876
Hey, what do you think you're doing,
Naruto?

400
00:22:26,900 --> 00:22:27,600
Just shut up and take care of it!

401
00:22:27,601 --> 00:22:29,121
That bird is only your responsibility!

402
00:22:29,660 --> 00:22:32,280
Stop doing that!

403
00:22:32,281 --> 00:22:33,281
Not your face!

404
00:22:33,700 --> 00:22:34,700
Stop it!

405
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:41,760
We'll find an inn for the night so we can
rest up.

406
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:44,220
Even Mr. Ostrich here looks worn out.

407
00:22:44,920 --> 00:22:45,880
All right.

408
00:22:45,900 --> 00:22:48,339
We could have made it
back to the village tonight

409
00:22:48,340 --> 00:22:51,201
if someone did a
better job with that bird.

410
00:22:54,740 --> 00:22:55,220
Huh?

411
00:22:55,221 --> 00:22:56,221
What's going on?

412
00:22:56,629 --> 00:22:57,900
I better go check it out!

413
00:22:58,144 --> 00:22:59,560
Hey, don't run off again!

414
00:23:01,860 --> 00:23:02,440
Let's go.

415
00:23:02,859 --> 00:23:03,860
What could be happening?

416
00:23:04,420 --> 00:23:05,740
Not you guys, too.

417
00:23:09,900 --> 00:23:11,000
It's just a fight?

418
00:23:11,460 --> 00:23:13,660
No, it seems to be a vendetta.

419
00:23:13,860 --> 00:23:14,740
A vendetta?

420
00:23:14,741 --> 00:23:18,640
Like when someone fights to get revenge or
to right a wrong?

421
00:23:20,755 --> 00:23:21,755
Revenge, huh?

422
00:23:22,360 --> 00:23:26,940
On a busy street in the middle of the day,
they allow that, Kakashi-sensei?

423
00:23:27,120 --> 00:23:28,120
Hmm.

424
00:23:28,240 --> 00:23:30,060
A vendetta permit, huh?

425
00:23:30,814 --> 00:23:35,040
It varies from village to village,
but sometimes if someone is murdered,

426
00:23:35,260 --> 00:23:37,180
family members are allowed to seek
revenge.

427
00:23:37,860 --> 00:23:40,579
If he has an authorized
permit from a land where the

428
00:23:40,580 --> 00:23:43,500
crime took place, other
nations will allow the vendetta.

429
00:23:44,549 --> 00:23:46,316
I heard that Tsukado,
the guy with the

430
00:23:46,317 --> 00:23:48,380
vendetta, had a distant
relative who was killed.

431
00:23:48,620 --> 00:23:51,440
Yeah, late one night his opponent went to
visit the victim.

432
00:23:52,124 --> 00:23:55,500
Then he ruthlessly hit Tsukado's relative
with a rock and killed him.

433
00:23:55,869 --> 00:23:57,280
It's an awful story, isn't it?

434
00:23:58,409 --> 00:24:00,800
Anyway, the killer escaped and the family
wanted revenge.

435
00:24:01,349 --> 00:24:02,820
They chose Tsukado to handle it.

436
00:24:05,239 --> 00:24:07,080
Then that coward deserves what he gets!

437
00:24:07,980 --> 00:24:10,060
Kanaboon, it looks like a vendetta,
boss.

438
00:24:11,080 --> 00:24:12,080
Hmm.

439
00:24:12,954 --> 00:24:13,954
Now this is interesting.

440
00:24:14,280 --> 00:24:15,880
Tell me what you think, boys.

441
00:24:16,020 --> 00:24:17,020
Who's gonna win?

442
00:24:17,259 --> 00:24:20,760
Well, I've heard it said that the hunter
is often stronger than the hunted.

443
00:24:21,320 --> 00:24:21,840
Heh.

444
00:24:22,120 --> 00:24:24,480
Nah, I can't go along with you on that
one.

445
00:24:25,069 --> 00:24:28,200
That hunted one has a pretty mean look
about him, if you ask me.

446
00:24:28,860 --> 00:24:29,860
Hmm.

447
00:24:36,930 --> 00:24:37,930
Aaaaah!

448
00:24:39,650 --> 00:24:40,170
Aaaaah!

449
00:24:40,630 --> 00:24:41,630
There they go!

450
00:24:41,790 --> 00:24:42,790
Oh no!

451
00:24:43,890 --> 00:24:45,190
What the...

452
00:24:49,870 --> 00:24:53,070
Looks like he won't be getting his revenge
today.

453
00:24:58,670 --> 00:25:00,230
What the hell?

454
00:25:03,610 --> 00:25:05,410
Hey, come back here!

455
00:25:05,670 --> 00:25:06,670
Hey, stop!

456
00:25:06,730 --> 00:25:07,930
Stop, you bastard!

457
00:25:12,970 --> 00:25:14,190
Damn you, bastard!

458
00:25:14,750 --> 00:25:15,230
Here.

459
00:25:15,730 --> 00:25:16,850
Oh, my sword.

460
00:25:17,090 --> 00:25:18,090
Thank you.

461
00:25:18,370 --> 00:25:20,230
He sure got lucky that time.

462
00:25:20,290 --> 00:25:21,310
I almost had him.

463
00:25:21,570 --> 00:25:22,050
Really?

464
00:25:22,170 --> 00:25:23,630
Cause it didn't look that way to me.

465
00:25:24,070 --> 00:25:24,510
Hmph.

466
00:25:25,009 --> 00:25:27,170
Amateurs should keep their opinions to
themselves.

467
00:25:27,570 --> 00:25:31,370
You can't tell by looking at me,
but I am the veteran of 34 vendettas.

468
00:25:31,590 --> 00:25:32,690
Oh, I see.

469
00:25:33,030 --> 00:25:34,030
Wait, what?

470
00:25:34,170 --> 00:25:36,610
You mean you failed at this 34 times?

471
00:25:36,750 --> 00:25:38,130
Next time for sure.

472
00:25:38,430 --> 00:25:39,490
I doubt that, bud!

473
00:25:40,079 --> 00:25:42,530
There is no way to know if I can win
unless I try.

474
00:25:42,531 --> 00:25:44,110
So I'll try again.

475
00:25:44,744 --> 00:25:47,910
You know what they say, 35th time's the
charm!

476
00:25:49,530 --> 00:25:50,530
Right.

477
00:25:51,374 --> 00:25:52,550
Okay, I get it!

478
00:25:53,210 --> 00:25:54,210
Huh?

479
00:25:54,319 --> 00:25:56,510
I'll help you and I won't take no for an
answer!

480
00:25:56,830 --> 00:25:56,990
Huh?

481
00:25:57,210 --> 00:25:57,730
Yeah!

482
00:25:58,179 --> 00:26:00,340
I'm gonna use every
single ninja skill I have

483
00:26:00,341 --> 00:26:03,171
to help you become
a real pro at vendettas!

484
00:26:05,150 --> 00:26:06,150
Huh?

485
00:26:06,190 --> 00:26:08,730
He's getting carried away again,
like always!

486
00:26:09,239 --> 00:26:12,430
Well, why don't we let Naruto handle this
one on his own?

487
00:26:12,679 --> 00:26:14,050
We can go rest up at the inn.

488
00:26:15,190 --> 00:26:16,190
Ridiculous.

489
00:26:16,949 --> 00:26:19,530
Leave it to me and that vendetta's as good
as done!

490
00:26:20,110 --> 00:26:21,110
Mm-mm.

491
00:26:24,630 --> 00:26:25,630
Lesson one!

492
00:26:26,210 --> 00:26:29,230
You don't have anywhere near enough anger
toward your enemy!

493
00:26:29,470 --> 00:26:33,250
You literally have to be ready to explode
with anger at any given moment!

494
00:26:33,830 --> 00:26:36,730
Cause then you'll never be caught off
guard for a vendetta!

495
00:26:37,090 --> 00:26:38,870
Uh, okay...

496
00:26:40,450 --> 00:26:41,850
Hey you, old lady!

497
00:26:42,430 --> 00:26:44,390
Look, you really need to be more careful!

498
00:26:44,670 --> 00:26:46,590
Come on, hurry up and get on my back!

499
00:26:46,870 --> 00:26:48,990
Now, tell me where you want to go,
dammit!

500
00:26:49,070 --> 00:26:50,310
The next town, huh?

501
00:26:50,510 --> 00:26:52,270
Alright, I'm glad to help out!

502
00:26:52,550 --> 00:26:54,590
Uh, that isn't... If it's
farther, that's fine!

503
00:26:55,630 --> 00:26:56,630
Oh boy...

504
00:26:58,450 --> 00:26:59,450
Lesson two!

505
00:26:59,970 --> 00:27:02,790
Take all vendettas seriously, even easy
ones!

506
00:27:02,970 --> 00:27:04,130
Get used to revenge!

507
00:27:05,850 --> 00:27:08,690
Uh... Excuse me, sir!

508
00:27:09,750 --> 00:27:11,190
I shall assist you.

509
00:27:11,191 --> 00:27:12,191
What?

510
00:27:12,870 --> 00:27:13,870
Ahhh!

511
00:27:14,430 --> 00:27:14,990
Ha!

512
00:27:15,130 --> 00:27:15,710
Take that!

513
00:27:15,790 --> 00:27:16,130
We'll cut it out!

514
00:27:16,131 --> 00:27:17,490
You stop it!

515
00:27:17,530 --> 00:27:18,850
That's not what I meant either!

516
00:27:18,851 --> 00:27:19,170
Think again!

517
00:27:19,370 --> 00:27:20,370
Quit it!

518
00:27:21,270 --> 00:27:22,890
Alright, lesson three!

519
00:27:23,604 --> 00:27:25,870
Completely fill your mind with pictures of
your enemy!

520
00:27:26,030 --> 00:27:28,250
And then put your anger down on paper!

521
00:27:28,730 --> 00:27:30,190
Uh-huh...

522
00:27:32,030 --> 00:27:33,030
What?

523
00:27:35,390 --> 00:27:36,650
What's wrong with you?

524
00:27:36,790 --> 00:27:40,050
You can't make your most hated enemy look
so nice at you!

525
00:27:41,509 --> 00:27:43,290
You know, I gotta say, mister...

526
00:27:43,639 --> 00:27:46,050
I don't really think you're cut out for
vendettas at all.

527
00:27:46,529 --> 00:27:48,830
Yeah, and you're not really cut out to be
a coach.

528
00:27:50,479 --> 00:27:51,610
Do you have to do it?

529
00:27:51,879 --> 00:27:52,910
Carry out the vendetta?

530
00:27:53,330 --> 00:27:54,330
I do.

531
00:27:54,649 --> 00:27:56,730
I can't go back to my village until it's
finished.

532
00:27:57,719 --> 00:28:00,310
I just want all of this to end,
so I can go home.

533
00:28:01,689 --> 00:28:03,530
My elderly mother and father need me.

534
00:28:06,999 --> 00:28:08,750
An ostrich is running wild!

535
00:28:10,050 --> 00:28:11,050
An ostrich?

536
00:28:18,644 --> 00:28:23,430
Whoa, mister... That swordsman...
he was hiding his skills.

537
00:28:23,820 --> 00:28:24,750
Alright, boys!

538
00:28:24,790 --> 00:28:25,790
Yes, sir!

539
00:28:26,870 --> 00:28:28,430
Time for some fun.

540
00:28:30,110 --> 00:28:32,910
Sorry, the ostrich bit through his leash.

541
00:28:34,810 --> 00:28:38,490
Just as I suspected, you are actually a
master swordsman.

542
00:28:38,690 --> 00:28:39,690
He's what?

543
00:28:40,450 --> 00:28:42,410
Hey, what's going on here?

544
00:28:42,570 --> 00:28:47,311
If you're really that good with your sword,
how come you can't finish your vendetta?

545
00:28:48,590 --> 00:28:49,610
I don't know.

546
00:28:49,730 --> 00:28:54,630
But whenever I look into his eyes,
all of my strength drains out of me.

547
00:28:56,690 --> 00:28:58,070
It's those eyes.

548
00:28:58,970 --> 00:29:00,450
Those piercing eyes.

549
00:29:03,390 --> 00:29:04,390
Mister...

550
00:29:08,650 --> 00:29:14,190
Ugh... I wonder where
that vendetta guy ran off to.

551
00:29:14,884 --> 00:29:17,890
He probably set out early in pursuit of
his enemy.

552
00:29:19,109 --> 00:29:21,570
Will he do that for the rest of his life?

553
00:29:24,824 --> 00:29:25,850
What's going on?

554
00:29:27,370 --> 00:29:29,710
Well, what do you think, mister vendetta?

555
00:29:29,950 --> 00:29:32,010
Your tenacity has won me over.

556
00:29:32,779 --> 00:29:36,690
I want to make sure you get your revenge,
so I brought your enemy right to you.

557
00:29:36,691 --> 00:29:40,750
I'm guessing you want to give him the
payback he deserves, right?

558
00:29:43,570 --> 00:29:44,570
Focus, mister.

559
00:29:44,870 --> 00:29:45,870
Wait.

560
00:29:46,050 --> 00:29:50,450
We, the Kanabun gang, will oversee this
vendetta and ensure its fairness.

561
00:29:50,630 --> 00:29:52,410
All right, everyone, here we go.

562
00:29:52,590 --> 00:29:54,290
Who do you think's gonna win?

563
00:29:54,530 --> 00:29:55,990
We're taking all bets.

564
00:29:56,530 --> 00:29:57,790
Which one's stronger?

565
00:29:58,250 --> 00:29:59,650
I say the one out for revenge.

566
00:30:00,130 --> 00:30:01,270
That guy's hopeless.

567
00:30:01,470 --> 00:30:02,470
The way he'll win.

568
00:30:02,630 --> 00:30:04,470
Well, I'm betting 500 on the other guy.

569
00:30:04,590 --> 00:30:05,590
Me too.

570
00:30:07,310 --> 00:30:11,730
If anyone's short on cash, the Kanabun
gang will place a bet for you.

571
00:30:12,370 --> 00:30:15,990
If that Tsukado guy uses his real
strength, this fight won't last a minute.

572
00:30:17,210 --> 00:30:19,390
Yeah, and we'll make a tidy profit.

573
00:30:19,850 --> 00:30:20,850
That's terrible.

574
00:30:21,310 --> 00:30:24,190
Those guys are just trying to make a buck
off this vendetta.

575
00:30:27,550 --> 00:30:29,190
It all ends right here.

576
00:30:29,970 --> 00:30:32,750
Sorry, but I'm not just going to lay down
and give up.

577
00:30:36,690 --> 00:30:37,690
On guard.

578
00:30:44,040 --> 00:30:44,800
What?

579
00:30:45,060 --> 00:30:47,760
He's trying to fight without looking his
opponent in the eye.

580
00:30:56,600 --> 00:30:58,160
He might actually win.

581
00:30:58,480 --> 00:31:01,040
Wait, did Naruto's lessons actually help?

582
00:31:06,150 --> 00:31:08,750
There's something about this fight that's
bugging me.

583
00:31:09,290 --> 00:31:10,290
Something's off.

584
00:31:10,710 --> 00:31:11,810
What is it?

585
00:31:15,010 --> 00:31:15,610
What's on the other side of his helmet?

586
00:31:15,611 --> 00:31:15,890
It's him.

587
00:31:16,250 --> 00:31:17,790
Just like Mister said.

588
00:31:18,090 --> 00:31:19,610
It's that guy's face.

589
00:31:19,930 --> 00:31:20,990
Those eyes.

590
00:31:29,790 --> 00:31:31,270
Those eyes again!

591
00:31:31,650 --> 00:31:33,630
How can you look at me like that?

592
00:31:33,890 --> 00:31:36,670
And you don't know that I could kill you!?

593
00:31:37,210 --> 00:31:38,210
B suck.

594
00:31:40,950 --> 00:31:42,150
Just give me a second.

595
00:31:56,490 --> 00:32:04,490
I know the reason why you couldn't kill
this guy.

596
00:32:05,079 --> 00:32:08,670
And I'm betting that somewhere deep down
inside of you, you know it too.

597
00:32:12,150 --> 00:32:13,150
Of course.

598
00:32:14,589 --> 00:32:15,610
I understand now.

599
00:32:16,650 --> 00:32:17,650
I see.

600
00:32:18,149 --> 00:32:19,450
His blade has been dulled.

601
00:32:20,419 --> 00:32:22,850
He couldn't kill anyone with it even if he
wanted to.

602
00:32:26,979 --> 00:32:27,979
Let me explain.

603
00:32:28,030 --> 00:32:30,610
I have a twin brother who is named Kageki.

604
00:32:31,639 --> 00:32:32,639
Are you serious?

605
00:32:32,750 --> 00:32:33,890
A twin brother?

606
00:32:34,190 --> 00:32:35,190
Yes.

607
00:32:35,439 --> 00:32:38,790
Kageki had loaned money to Shikazo,
a member of your clan.

608
00:32:40,250 --> 00:32:43,216
But then my brother had
a child and needed money

609
00:32:43,217 --> 00:32:46,231
quickly, so he went to
Shikazo to ask to be repaid.

610
00:32:46,899 --> 00:32:50,190
Shikazo ignored my brother and tried to
back out of his debt.

611
00:32:51,250 --> 00:32:56,150
They argued, a scuffle broke out between
them, and they both fell to the dirt floor.

612
00:32:56,709 --> 00:32:59,830
But when he fell, Shikazo hit his head on
a stone.

613
00:33:01,009 --> 00:33:02,009
And then he died.

614
00:33:02,124 --> 00:33:04,730
Are you saying it was all just an
accident?

615
00:33:05,539 --> 00:33:07,550
Kageki said that he'd turn himself in.

616
00:33:07,551 --> 00:33:10,210
But there were no witnesses to back him
up.

617
00:33:11,050 --> 00:33:14,470
Given the circumstances, he probably would
have been accused of murder.

618
00:33:15,009 --> 00:33:16,910
So I offered to switch places with him.

619
00:33:17,365 --> 00:33:18,430
You did what?

620
00:33:18,810 --> 00:33:20,970
I assumed my twin brother's identity.

621
00:33:21,290 --> 00:33:23,905
And then I told him, his
wife, and their newborn

622
00:33:23,906 --> 00:33:26,190
child to go into hiding
to keep them all safe.

623
00:33:26,560 --> 00:33:29,263
In order to buy them
time to escape, I purposely

624
00:33:29,264 --> 00:33:32,211
attracted the attention
of the pursuers.

625
00:33:32,529 --> 00:33:35,290
I couldn't let a great guy like him ruin
his own life.

626
00:33:35,790 --> 00:33:37,510
Not when I'm such a scoundrel.

627
00:33:37,550 --> 00:33:40,630
Who's caused nothing but grief to my
family, and to society.

628
00:33:41,530 --> 00:33:43,770
I guess I figured that this would be a
way...

629
00:33:44,640 --> 00:33:46,230
To atone for all that.

630
00:33:47,339 --> 00:33:49,310
I only have my brother's word about it.

631
00:33:50,170 --> 00:33:52,530
There's no way for me to prove that's what
happened.

632
00:33:52,850 --> 00:33:55,050
But I believe that what he said is true.

633
00:33:55,610 --> 00:33:56,610
Hm.

634
00:33:57,090 --> 00:33:58,090
Mister?

635
00:34:00,319 --> 00:34:02,930
But it's up to you whether you want to
believe me or not.

636
00:34:03,749 --> 00:34:05,350
And if you don't believe me...

637
00:34:06,469 --> 00:34:07,469
Then you can kill me.

638
00:34:11,480 --> 00:34:14,260
I'm going to choose to believe that what
you say is the truth.

639
00:34:14,540 --> 00:34:15,841
You... Yeah, Mister!

640
00:34:16,530 --> 00:34:19,219
Frankly, I'm sick and tired of this thing
called revenge.

641
00:34:20,470 --> 00:34:23,280
If you've pretended all these years to be
my enemy...

642
00:34:24,080 --> 00:34:26,760
Well then, I'll just pretend to be on a
vendetta.

643
00:34:28,760 --> 00:34:29,760
Thank you.

644
00:34:35,070 --> 00:34:37,860
You think everything turned out okay,
Kakashi-sensei?

645
00:34:38,380 --> 00:34:38,940
Well...

646
00:34:39,040 --> 00:34:40,679
That's for those two to decide.

647
00:34:42,070 --> 00:34:45,120
I guess revenge is really complicated,
isn't it?

648
00:34:45,340 --> 00:34:46,340
Hmph.

649
00:34:46,400 --> 00:34:47,560
What would you know about it?

650
00:34:48,100 --> 00:34:49,100
Huh?

651
00:34:49,415 --> 00:34:52,679
Sometimes a vendetta must be carried out
no matter how hard it is.

652
00:34:57,020 --> 00:34:58,020
Hey.

653
00:35:02,440 --> 00:35:04,640
How'd you figure out we were tailing him,
huh?

654
00:35:05,160 --> 00:35:07,120
Maybe there were just too many of us.

655
00:35:07,280 --> 00:35:07,920
Oh, please.

656
00:35:08,040 --> 00:35:11,200
If you know how to hide, it doesn't matter
how many people there are.

657
00:35:11,940 --> 00:35:14,800
Don't tell me you've forgotten all of your
jutsu, Sakura!

658
00:35:15,060 --> 00:35:16,680
You're the one who forgets!

659
00:35:16,700 --> 00:35:17,860
We should shadow him.

660
00:35:17,980 --> 00:35:18,980
It'll be good practice.

661
00:35:19,930 --> 00:35:21,540
But we should do it solo this time.

662
00:35:21,930 --> 00:35:23,440
Yeah, I think so too.

663
00:35:23,770 --> 00:35:25,280
We should totally ditch Naruto.

664
00:35:25,740 --> 00:35:26,740
Say what?!

665
00:35:28,814 --> 00:35:29,814
Hmm...

666
00:35:30,500 --> 00:35:32,400
Forlorn, Junko fell on him.

667
00:35:32,920 --> 00:35:36,260
I'm losing you, and in doing so,
I am lost.

668
00:35:44,380 --> 00:35:45,380
Huh?

669
00:35:45,640 --> 00:35:45,800
Huh?

670
00:35:45,801 --> 00:35:48,020
What the... Hey!

671
00:35:48,220 --> 00:35:50,621
I... Wha... Ah!

672
00:35:54,950 --> 00:35:55,950
Hm?

673
00:35:56,195 --> 00:35:59,790
He got away.

674
00:36:00,370 --> 00:36:02,310
Just as clumsy as always.

675
00:36:02,760 --> 00:36:04,230
Why are you such an idiot?

676
00:36:04,650 --> 00:36:06,291
Ugh... Ugh...

677
00:36:06,590 --> 00:36:07,370
Hm?

678
00:36:07,590 --> 00:36:07,930
Hm?

679
00:36:08,130 --> 00:36:09,130
Hm?

680
00:36:09,230 --> 00:36:10,230
Hm?

681
00:36:11,270 --> 00:36:11,690
Hm?

682
00:36:11,691 --> 00:36:14,070
What?

683
00:36:14,071 --> 00:36:15,071
Kikiki!

684
00:36:15,510 --> 00:36:17,911
Wh... Huh?

685
00:36:20,190 --> 00:36:21,190
Right...

686
00:36:23,130 --> 00:36:24,670
Don't you see!

687
00:36:28,150 --> 00:36:30,590
What is he doing?

688
00:36:30,810 --> 00:36:34,010
Ugh... Huh?

689
00:36:34,350 --> 00:36:35,830
What is he doing?

690
00:36:35,831 --> 00:36:36,730
What?

691
00:36:36,731 --> 00:36:39,510
Huh?

692
00:36:44,360 --> 00:36:45,760
Huh?

693
00:36:45,940 --> 00:36:46,400
Huh?

694
00:36:46,401 --> 00:36:47,780
Sasuke, how'd it go?

695
00:36:49,530 --> 00:36:51,520
I got tired of shadowing him.

696
00:36:59,569 --> 00:37:02,950
Listen and enjoy, people of the Leaf
Village.

697
00:37:04,685 --> 00:37:06,763
I've come to provide a
moment's respite from

698
00:37:06,764 --> 00:37:09,531
life's hardships with some
festive song and dance.

699
00:37:18,280 --> 00:37:19,280
Honore...

700
00:37:35,480 --> 00:37:37,160
Good job on that mission, guys.

701
00:37:37,730 --> 00:37:38,860
Yeah, we're great.

702
00:37:39,115 --> 00:37:42,380
But what's really great is that I can
finally get some Ichiraku ramen.

703
00:37:42,660 --> 00:37:43,920
That does sound good.

704
00:37:44,325 --> 00:37:45,900
Naruto, it's your treat, right?

705
00:37:46,080 --> 00:37:46,320
What?

706
00:37:46,880 --> 00:37:47,880
Oh, alright.

707
00:37:48,020 --> 00:37:49,020
I guess so.

708
00:37:49,215 --> 00:37:49,940
Wait a sec.

709
00:37:50,100 --> 00:37:52,560
Sasuke, how about you treating us for
once?

710
00:37:52,880 --> 00:37:53,160
Huh.

711
00:37:53,470 --> 00:37:55,280
I'm gonna go train, not eat.

712
00:37:55,540 --> 00:37:57,640
What about you, Kakashi-sensei?

713
00:38:10,540 --> 00:38:11,660
I'm gonna go train, not eat.

714
00:38:12,120 --> 00:38:13,920
That woman is so beautiful.

715
00:38:14,580 --> 00:38:16,260
And a criminal, apparently.

716
00:38:23,100 --> 00:38:26,462
I've heard she's a Kunoichi
who disguised herself as a street

717
00:38:26,463 --> 00:38:29,400
performer so she could
gather intel on the land of fire.

718
00:38:30,160 --> 00:38:31,940
So she's actually a spy?

719
00:38:32,360 --> 00:38:33,360
What happens now?

720
00:38:33,760 --> 00:38:38,100
Well, she'll be interrogated so we can
discover exactly what she learned.

721
00:38:38,484 --> 00:38:42,400
They'll use any and all means at their
disposal until she confirms it.

722
00:38:42,401 --> 00:38:43,921
And then she confesses what she knows.

723
00:39:02,830 --> 00:39:03,830
Welcome, come in.

724
00:39:04,595 --> 00:39:06,160
We call this the Honesty Room.

725
00:39:16,920 --> 00:39:17,920
Hmm.

726
00:39:18,750 --> 00:39:20,979
She must be quite well
trained indeed if she's

727
00:39:20,980 --> 00:39:23,841
able to resist your
interrogation techniques.

728
00:39:24,180 --> 00:39:25,660
Not one scream escaped her.

729
00:39:26,250 --> 00:39:28,360
All we heard was the sound of her gritting
her teeth.

730
00:39:29,725 --> 00:39:32,120
My, what an impressive Kunoichi.

731
00:39:33,100 --> 00:39:34,974
Well then, we'll just
have to reach into that

732
00:39:34,975 --> 00:39:37,961
silence and listen to
her inner voice instead.

733
00:39:38,180 --> 00:39:39,280
I understand, sir.

734
00:39:40,310 --> 00:39:41,440
Please summon him for me.

735
00:39:46,390 --> 00:39:47,390
Clouds.

736
00:39:47,695 --> 00:39:48,750
They look like clouds.

737
00:39:50,680 --> 00:39:53,670
Just like the ones we saw that day.

738
00:39:59,550 --> 00:40:01,010
We're all finished using pain.

739
00:40:01,920 --> 00:40:03,350
It's time for a gentler approach.

740
00:40:34,040 --> 00:40:35,240
Now, Hanare.

741
00:40:35,600 --> 00:40:38,481
Your task is to infiltrate
the Land of Fire and

742
00:40:38,482 --> 00:40:41,140
report back on the
state of affairs in the Leaf.

743
00:40:41,820 --> 00:40:43,900
I'm to go to the Hidden Leaf Village?

744
00:40:44,500 --> 00:40:48,400
Our nation has survived all these years
not because of our military might,

745
00:40:48,560 --> 00:40:50,840
but rather due to our skill at espionage.

746
00:40:51,920 --> 00:40:56,960
We gather all of the information we can
from the other nations, use it to plan

747
00:40:56,961 --> 00:41:00,460
strategies, and gain advantage over
opponents in negotiations.

748
00:41:01,100 --> 00:41:03,200
That way, we can avert potential
conflicts.

749
00:41:03,980 --> 00:41:07,040
The fate of our nation now rests in your
hands, Hanare.

750
00:41:07,340 --> 00:41:08,100
Yes, sir.

751
00:41:08,220 --> 00:41:09,440
I will not fail.

752
00:41:19,560 --> 00:41:20,560
What's that?

753
00:41:21,320 --> 00:41:22,340
That headband?

754
00:41:23,380 --> 00:41:24,960
The Hidden Lock Village.

755
00:41:25,680 --> 00:41:27,080
In the Land of Ki.

756
00:41:55,930 --> 00:41:59,090
We captured her before she was able to
reach the Leaf Village.

757
00:41:59,910 --> 00:42:01,730
She didn't learn anything of importance.

758
00:42:03,910 --> 00:42:08,690
And now, it's my turn to get some intel on
your village and why you were sent here.

759
00:42:24,420 --> 00:42:25,420
What's going on?

760
00:42:26,240 --> 00:42:28,720
Why doesn't she have any memories of her
own village?

761
00:42:35,820 --> 00:42:36,920
It was nothing.

762
00:42:58,900 --> 00:42:59,900
What?

763
00:43:02,820 --> 00:43:04,320
Memories of me as a child?

764
00:43:05,140 --> 00:43:06,140
Yeah.

765
00:43:06,550 --> 00:43:07,950
Do you remember anything about her?

766
00:43:08,340 --> 00:43:09,340
No.

767
00:43:09,710 --> 00:43:10,750
I've never met her before.

768
00:43:12,880 --> 00:43:13,880
Oh, I see.

769
00:43:15,470 --> 00:43:16,590
Did you learn anything else?

770
00:43:17,580 --> 00:43:18,580
Nothing significant.

771
00:43:19,680 --> 00:43:22,200
She seems to have no memories of the
Hidden Lock Village at all.

772
00:43:23,470 --> 00:43:24,830
I'm guessing that she purged them.

773
00:43:25,340 --> 00:43:26,340
Purged them?

774
00:43:28,120 --> 00:43:30,160
But something else is bothering me.

775
00:43:30,360 --> 00:43:32,460
Something I can't quite put my finger on.

776
00:43:32,859 --> 00:43:35,700
And it's more than just the fact that she
had memories of you.

777
00:43:36,140 --> 00:43:37,160
She's hiding something.

778
00:43:37,920 --> 00:43:39,460
Something even I can't dig up.

779
00:43:39,669 --> 00:43:40,780
I'm baffled.

780
00:43:42,570 --> 00:43:43,570
That's why you're here.

781
00:43:43,840 --> 00:43:45,760
I need your help with this, Kakashi.

782
00:43:46,200 --> 00:43:46,680
Huh?

783
00:43:47,180 --> 00:43:48,180
Me?

784
00:43:48,670 --> 00:43:50,540
But I'm not a member of the intel
division.

785
00:43:52,650 --> 00:43:55,240
You might be able to see deeper into her
psyche than we can.

786
00:44:18,240 --> 00:44:19,790
You must be some kind of fool.

787
00:44:20,540 --> 00:44:23,890
You're showing me around the very village
I infiltrated to spy on.

788
00:44:24,490 --> 00:44:27,350
You won't see anything here you wouldn't
see in any other village.

789
00:44:28,100 --> 00:44:31,170
And I thought you could use some air after
being in that stuffy room.

790
00:44:39,420 --> 00:44:40,420
Hmm.

791
00:44:45,960 --> 00:44:47,880
Which flower should I choose?

792
00:44:49,380 --> 00:44:50,380
What?

793
00:44:51,980 --> 00:44:52,980
What?

794
00:44:54,480 --> 00:44:55,480
No way!

795
00:44:55,900 --> 00:44:57,520
Wait a minute, what did you just say?

796
00:44:57,720 --> 00:44:59,780
Oh my, Kakashi-sensei!

797
00:45:07,930 --> 00:45:08,930
Kakashi's with her?

798
00:45:10,050 --> 00:45:11,710
So you're curious too, huh?

799
00:45:11,711 --> 00:45:13,250
It's not like that, you idiot.

800
00:45:13,530 --> 00:45:13,810
Hey!

801
00:45:13,950 --> 00:45:14,950
It's that woman!

802
00:45:15,250 --> 00:45:16,990
What's he doing with someone like her?

803
00:45:18,830 --> 00:45:19,830
Hey!

804
00:45:49,280 --> 00:45:50,760
You don't have to keep your distance.

805
00:45:51,110 --> 00:45:53,440
I promise I won't try to get information
out of you.

806
00:45:54,580 --> 00:45:56,400
I was just asked to spend the day with
you.

807
00:45:56,640 --> 00:45:57,640
That's all.

808
00:45:58,580 --> 00:46:00,940
And once the day is done, so is my
assignment.

809
00:46:02,330 --> 00:46:03,380
What will happen to me?

810
00:46:04,100 --> 00:46:05,100
I don't know.

811
00:46:06,820 --> 00:46:09,740
That cloud... looks like Naruto to me.

812
00:46:10,740 --> 00:46:13,620
And next to that one is... Sasuke,
maybe.

813
00:46:14,420 --> 00:46:15,420
Serious?

814
00:46:17,445 --> 00:46:21,600
When I look at the clouds, I see my mother
and father who gave life to me.

815
00:46:22,660 --> 00:46:24,200
Although I never knew them.

816
00:46:24,800 --> 00:46:29,700
When things were hard, when I was sad,
I'd always look up at the clouds.

817
00:46:30,260 --> 00:46:33,220
I'd stare at them and let my imagination
run free.

818
00:46:33,855 --> 00:46:36,283
I'd daydream about
the village where I was

819
00:46:36,284 --> 00:46:38,940
born, and imagine what
my parents might be like.

820
00:46:39,360 --> 00:46:42,390
Those daydreams helped
me endure my loneliness,

821
00:46:42,391 --> 00:46:45,281
and the pain of not
knowing a home or family.

822
00:46:46,690 --> 00:46:49,980
It was the only way I could accept being
just a spy.

823
00:46:52,760 --> 00:46:54,520
I can't hear anything!

824
00:46:55,140 --> 00:46:58,260
They both seem so perfect for each other,
don't they?

825
00:46:59,380 --> 00:46:59,980
Ridiculous.

826
00:47:00,240 --> 00:47:02,440
I'm gonna get closer so I can hear!

827
00:47:02,740 --> 00:47:04,560
I wasn't allowed to have a home.

828
00:47:04,840 --> 00:47:07,761
I was raised outside the
village, so that I couldn't

829
00:47:07,762 --> 00:47:10,400
divulge any information
about it if I were captured.

830
00:47:12,255 --> 00:47:15,212
All this time, I've risked
my life on missions

831
00:47:15,213 --> 00:47:18,101
for a homeland that I've
never even seen before.

832
00:47:19,434 --> 00:47:23,840
That's why having a home and people who
accept me is so important.

833
00:47:31,110 --> 00:47:34,710
Why are you telling me all this now,
when you've been silent all day?

834
00:47:38,700 --> 00:47:40,700
Because... there's something that you've
taught me.

835
00:47:40,880 --> 00:47:47,150
I knew the moment I saw you... that you
were the boy from my past.

836
00:47:52,390 --> 00:47:54,550
I had decided to meet my parents.

837
00:47:55,240 --> 00:47:56,270
And so I set out.

838
00:47:56,271 --> 00:47:57,271
I set out for my village.

839
00:47:57,710 --> 00:47:58,850
But I got lost.

840
00:47:59,325 --> 00:48:01,370
I was feeling helpless when we met.

841
00:48:10,100 --> 00:48:15,380
You told me that... whenever I was feeling
sad, I should look up at the clouds.

842
00:48:16,200 --> 00:48:20,620
That as the clouds changed shape,
I could turn them into whatever I wanted.

843
00:48:21,410 --> 00:48:23,382
You promised me that
as long as I had hope,

844
00:48:23,383 --> 00:48:26,421
the clouds would give
me the comfort I needed.

845
00:48:38,630 --> 00:48:42,170
From then on... I searched
the clouds for your likeness.

846
00:48:43,410 --> 00:48:45,110
That's why I recognized you right away.

847
00:48:45,550 --> 00:48:47,550
Even though time had changed you.

848
00:48:48,530 --> 00:48:50,850
Because you've always been in my heart.

849
00:48:52,530 --> 00:48:54,930
You gave me hope when things were darkest.

850
00:48:57,470 --> 00:48:58,470
Whoa!

851
00:48:58,530 --> 00:49:00,630
Things are really starting to heat up!

852
00:49:01,630 --> 00:49:02,230
Careful!

853
00:49:02,550 --> 00:49:04,351
Or else they'll... Whoa!

854
00:49:15,505 --> 00:49:16,790
What are you three doing?

855
00:49:16,990 --> 00:49:19,490
Oh, well, you see, Narza...
Hey, what are you doing?

856
00:49:19,650 --> 00:49:20,070
Let's go!

857
00:49:20,190 --> 00:49:20,710
There you go!

858
00:49:20,930 --> 00:49:21,930
Congratulations!

859
00:49:22,830 --> 00:49:23,830
Huh?

860
00:49:26,550 --> 00:49:27,550
Thank you.

861
00:49:39,295 --> 00:49:44,240
We've received news that the Hidden Lock
has captured Riichi, one of our Jonin.

862
00:49:44,810 --> 00:49:45,810
The Hidden Lock Village.

863
00:49:46,410 --> 00:49:47,840
We think the spy comes from there.

864
00:49:47,960 --> 00:49:48,960
That Kunoichi.

865
00:49:49,780 --> 00:49:50,780
Yes, Hanare.

866
00:49:50,980 --> 00:49:54,760
And the Lock Village has proposed that we
exchange her for Riichi.

867
00:49:55,700 --> 00:49:59,213
Fortunately for us, it appears
that she's gathered very little

868
00:49:59,214 --> 00:50:02,280
information about the Land
of Fire and our Leaf Village.

869
00:50:03,020 --> 00:50:04,820
So releasing her would be harmless.

870
00:50:05,260 --> 00:50:06,260
Huh?

871
00:50:06,545 --> 00:50:07,300
No, you can't.

872
00:50:07,400 --> 00:50:10,980
I mean... I'm completely opposed to giving
her back.

873
00:50:11,220 --> 00:50:12,220
Hm?

874
00:50:30,920 --> 00:50:32,620
It's not a transformation, Jutsu!

875
00:50:32,621 --> 00:50:33,900
That's Riichi!

876
00:50:34,120 --> 00:50:35,120
Without a doubt!

877
00:50:35,540 --> 00:50:36,540
Hm.

878
00:50:37,340 --> 00:50:38,340
All right, then!

879
00:50:38,930 --> 00:50:43,401
One man from each side will accompany
their prisoner to the center of the bridge!

880
00:50:43,515 --> 00:50:45,155
And that's where we'll make the exchange!

881
00:50:45,660 --> 00:50:46,660
Agreed?

882
00:50:47,654 --> 00:50:48,654
Agreed.

883
00:50:54,170 --> 00:50:55,290
Kakashi-sensei...

884
00:50:55,690 --> 00:50:57,250
I never thought it would end like this.

885
00:51:27,500 --> 00:51:29,000
I won't let you go.

886
00:51:37,720 --> 00:51:38,720
Hanare!

887
00:51:39,460 --> 00:51:42,180
Make sure you bring back the intel on the
hidden leaf!

888
00:51:46,080 --> 00:51:47,080
Retreat!

889
00:51:51,770 --> 00:51:52,290
Quick!

890
00:51:52,410 --> 00:51:53,410
It's already started!

891
00:52:02,800 --> 00:52:03,720
Give it up!

892
00:52:03,740 --> 00:52:05,040
There's no escape, old man!

893
00:52:07,240 --> 00:52:09,800
Don't underestimate the ninja of the lock.

894
00:52:10,080 --> 00:52:14,120
Once a key turns the lock closed,
not even death can open it!

895
00:52:20,460 --> 00:52:24,400
The blade of the deadly knife is never a
secret!

896
00:52:24,401 --> 00:52:25,000
I am out of here!

897
00:52:25,120 --> 00:52:26,120
Take that!

898
00:53:09,220 --> 00:53:10,500
Kagashi-sensei!

899
00:53:12,740 --> 00:53:13,700
You scared me!

900
00:53:13,701 --> 00:53:14,701
Where's Hanare?

901
00:53:15,920 --> 00:53:19,320
I guess she felt cornered and had no other
recourse.

902
00:53:19,800 --> 00:53:21,420
She threw herself off the cliff.

903
00:53:22,370 --> 00:53:24,360
She was an admirable ninja.

904
00:53:24,361 --> 00:53:26,020
She did what?

905
00:53:26,080 --> 00:53:29,580
But you... you can't be okay with this,
Kakashi-sensei.

906
00:53:29,620 --> 00:53:32,007
I mean, what if that
lady really was in love

907
00:53:32,008 --> 00:53:33,980
with you, and you guys
could have... Enough.

908
00:53:34,520 --> 00:53:36,020
It doesn't matter now.

909
00:54:03,160 --> 00:54:04,500
Off we go!

910
00:54:05,740 --> 00:54:08,080
Our mission is helping out at a farm.

911
00:54:08,500 --> 00:54:11,060
The mission itself's no big deal.

912
00:54:11,061 --> 00:54:13,700
No matter what happens, we're gonna see
it!

913
00:54:13,980 --> 00:54:16,060
Kakashi-sensei's real face!

914
00:54:18,720 --> 00:54:20,440
What's with you guys today?

915
00:54:20,740 --> 00:54:22,360
You seem ready for anything.

916
00:54:22,840 --> 00:54:24,440
Oh, we're ready, alright!

917
00:54:26,000 --> 00:54:27,120
Alrighty then.

918
00:54:27,280 --> 00:54:28,340
Good to hear.

919
00:54:32,580 --> 00:54:35,520
So, I've finally found you.

920
00:54:37,740 --> 00:54:39,080
Kakashi Hatake.

921
00:54:40,640 --> 00:54:41,840
Oh, Kakashi.

922
00:54:42,320 --> 00:54:44,320
It's been a long time.

923
00:54:44,900 --> 00:54:48,380
But my revenge is finally at hand.

924
00:54:48,680 --> 00:54:49,320
Your revenge?

925
00:54:49,380 --> 00:54:50,380
For what, boss?

926
00:54:50,700 --> 00:54:51,780
You fool!

927
00:54:51,880 --> 00:54:52,880
Have you forgotten?

928
00:54:53,940 --> 00:54:55,660
Well, I haven't.

929
00:54:55,661 --> 00:54:58,220
It was three years ago, in the spring.

930
00:54:58,900 --> 00:54:59,900
No!

931
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:02,180
There's no need to be frightened!

932
00:55:02,780 --> 00:55:03,780
No!

933
00:55:04,400 --> 00:55:07,380
Our boss says he has something he needs to
talk to you about.

934
00:55:09,300 --> 00:55:10,300
Your boss?

935
00:55:20,740 --> 00:55:22,220
I love you.

936
00:55:22,760 --> 00:55:24,380
Marry me, I beg of you.

937
00:55:24,640 --> 00:55:25,240
Wow, boss!

938
00:55:25,241 --> 00:55:26,241
You're the man!

939
00:55:27,460 --> 00:55:28,960
Don't be shy now.

940
00:55:29,600 --> 00:55:33,460
Embrace your emotions, my flower,
and fly to my bazooka!

941
00:55:33,461 --> 00:55:33,700
What?

942
00:55:34,280 --> 00:55:35,980
No, thanks.

943
00:55:36,740 --> 00:55:38,120
Don't worry, darling.

944
00:55:38,380 --> 00:55:41,840
Even if you don't like what you see,
I'm filthy rich!

945
00:55:42,180 --> 00:55:43,340
I said no, okay?

946
00:55:43,840 --> 00:55:44,840
What?

947
00:55:45,000 --> 00:55:47,400
How could you possibly refuse me?

948
00:55:48,000 --> 00:55:49,640
No means no!

949
00:55:50,840 --> 00:55:51,440
What?

950
00:55:51,715 --> 00:55:54,080
I arranged such romantic settings.

951
00:55:54,360 --> 00:55:55,880
What part of no don't you understand?

952
00:55:56,340 --> 00:55:58,320
I think this has gone on long enough.

953
00:55:58,560 --> 00:55:59,560
Huh?

954
00:56:00,300 --> 00:56:01,300
Howdy-do.

955
00:56:01,740 --> 00:56:04,240
Look, it doesn't matter how you slice it.

956
00:56:04,340 --> 00:56:05,900
I don't think the lady's interested.

957
00:56:06,519 --> 00:56:08,400
Rejection hurts, but what can you do?

958
00:56:09,140 --> 00:56:11,100
You got a lot of nerve there, pal!

959
00:56:11,500 --> 00:56:14,160
I don't think you grasp who you're dealing
with.

960
00:56:15,120 --> 00:56:17,635
You're tangling with
the Moya Triad, ninja trio

961
00:56:17,636 --> 00:56:20,481
that strikes fear in
the hearts of children!

962
00:56:21,480 --> 00:56:22,480
Moya Triad?

963
00:56:22,860 --> 00:56:23,900
Never heard of you.

964
00:56:24,120 --> 00:56:26,060
Never heard of a Moya Triad?

965
00:56:26,340 --> 00:56:28,020
You dare to mock us?

966
00:56:28,100 --> 00:56:29,320
Who do you think you are?

967
00:56:29,321 --> 00:56:30,820
Who, me?

968
00:56:31,100 --> 00:56:32,980
The name's Kakashi Hatake.

969
00:56:33,380 --> 00:56:34,900
I'm hardly worth mentioning.

970
00:56:35,160 --> 00:56:36,600
So why'd you even bother?

971
00:56:36,780 --> 00:56:37,780
No good scum!

972
00:56:37,840 --> 00:56:39,160
You'll live to regret this!

973
00:56:39,460 --> 00:56:42,600
You should know better than to meddle in a
man's quest for love.

974
00:56:43,080 --> 00:56:44,320
Quest for love?

975
00:56:44,720 --> 00:56:46,820
You mean stalking, don't you?

976
00:56:47,860 --> 00:56:49,200
Hold your tongue!

977
00:56:49,960 --> 00:56:52,120
All right, boys, time to dance.

978
00:56:52,300 --> 00:56:52,580
Right!

979
00:56:53,080 --> 00:56:55,360
Four, three, two, one!

980
00:56:55,900 --> 00:56:56,500
Hustle!

981
00:56:56,680 --> 00:56:57,280
Hustle!

982
00:56:57,500 --> 00:56:58,500
Yeah!

983
00:56:59,320 --> 00:57:00,320
Ow!

984
00:57:01,420 --> 00:57:02,420
Hey,

985
00:57:05,260 --> 00:57:06,800
come on, little help over here!

986
00:57:07,100 --> 00:57:09,060
Seriously, I'm pretty scared of heights!

987
00:57:09,061 --> 00:57:10,421
I'll take you back to the village.

988
00:57:11,020 --> 00:57:12,140
Darling, where are you?

989
00:57:12,460 --> 00:57:14,000
Are you just gonna leave us up here?

990
00:57:16,940 --> 00:57:19,200
So anyway, that's how it all went down.

991
00:57:19,420 --> 00:57:20,060
Don't gloat!

992
00:57:20,061 --> 00:57:21,080
You're the one who lost!

993
00:57:21,720 --> 00:57:24,220
So now we're gonna get payback for three
years ago.

994
00:57:24,760 --> 00:57:26,660
The boss has only gotten stronger.

995
00:57:27,020 --> 00:57:29,300
He'll crush that chump into dust if they
go to hell.

996
00:57:29,301 --> 00:57:29,720
I'm not gonna let you go toe-to-toe!

997
00:57:29,780 --> 00:57:31,500
The suspense is killing me!

998
00:57:32,000 --> 00:57:33,300
You dingbat!

999
00:57:33,500 --> 00:57:35,360
I'm not gonna stick my neck out like that!

1000
00:57:35,680 --> 00:57:36,680
Huh?

1001
00:57:36,920 --> 00:57:40,360
If I'm going to do this, it will be from
the shadows.

1002
00:57:43,080 --> 00:57:44,520
That's, uh, pretty dirty.

1003
00:57:44,940 --> 00:57:45,440
Ah-ho!

1004
00:57:45,860 --> 00:57:46,880
Ah-ho!

1005
00:57:47,640 --> 00:57:48,660
Oh, welcome!

1006
00:57:49,080 --> 00:57:50,080
My, my, my!

1007
00:57:50,120 --> 00:57:50,620
Welcome!

1008
00:57:50,980 --> 00:57:51,580
Welcome!

1009
00:57:51,920 --> 00:57:52,920
Welcome!

1010
00:57:53,860 --> 00:57:54,860
Yeah!

1011
00:57:56,720 --> 00:57:57,320
Oh!

1012
00:57:57,321 --> 00:57:58,321
Wow!

1013
00:57:58,420 --> 00:57:59,680
Oh, wow!

1014
00:58:00,420 --> 00:58:01,840
That looks good!

1015
00:58:02,240 --> 00:58:03,240
How lavish.

1016
00:58:04,890 --> 00:58:06,300
Take your time!

1017
00:58:12,260 --> 00:58:16,740
Enjoy your meal, Kakashi, for it will be
your last.

1018
00:58:16,980 --> 00:58:20,334
I've added a tasteless
and odorless narcotic to

1019
00:58:20,335 --> 00:58:23,600
your food that brings
on uncontrollable hiccups.

1020
00:58:24,110 --> 00:58:26,900
Dig in, my friend, and hiccup till you
die!

1021
00:58:29,440 --> 00:58:32,160
A fitting end for one such as you.

1022
00:58:35,040 --> 00:58:36,040
Hm?

1023
00:58:36,330 --> 00:58:37,610
What's the matter with you guys?

1024
00:58:37,950 --> 00:58:39,430
No one's picking up their chopsticks.

1025
00:58:39,900 --> 00:58:40,900
Oh, it's nothing.

1026
00:58:41,040 --> 00:58:43,060
Don't wait on us, Kakashi-sensei.

1027
00:58:43,061 --> 00:58:44,061
You go ahead and eat.

1028
00:58:44,590 --> 00:58:47,280
Actually, I'm kind of on a diet right now.

1029
00:58:47,910 --> 00:58:49,900
So that's how he wants to play it,
huh?

1030
00:58:50,160 --> 00:58:51,960
Well, I don't care what it takes.

1031
00:58:52,100 --> 00:58:53,680
That mask is coming off!

1032
00:58:54,040 --> 00:58:54,920
Oh, no!

1033
00:58:55,020 --> 00:58:56,020
My hand slipped!

1034
00:58:57,060 --> 00:58:58,060
Aaaaaaah!

1035
00:58:59,600 --> 00:59:00,600
Aaaaaaah!

1036
00:59:02,620 --> 00:59:03,260
Aaaaaaah!

1037
00:59:03,261 --> 00:59:04,261
Aaaaaaah!

1038
00:59:04,520 --> 00:59:05,520
Aaaaaaah!

1039
00:59:06,180 --> 00:59:07,180
Aaaaaaah!

1040
00:59:10,300 --> 00:59:10,940
Aaaaaaah!

1041
00:59:11,160 --> 00:59:11,780
Aaaaaaah!

1042
00:59:11,781 --> 00:59:13,020
Are you out of your mind?

1043
00:59:13,360 --> 00:59:14,240
Sorry about that.

1044
00:59:14,300 --> 00:59:15,340
My hand just slipped.

1045
00:59:15,620 --> 00:59:17,300
What do you mean your hand slipped?

1046
00:59:17,740 --> 00:59:18,840
Oh, no!

1047
00:59:19,080 --> 00:59:20,280
All our cooking!

1048
00:59:20,600 --> 00:59:22,440
How could he do such a thing?

1049
00:59:23,160 --> 00:59:24,160
Ugh!

1050
00:59:25,740 --> 00:59:27,760
Okay, what's our next move, guys?

1051
00:59:28,020 --> 00:59:29,240
Don't worry about it.

1052
00:59:29,300 --> 00:59:30,460
I think I have a plan.

1053
00:59:31,230 --> 00:59:32,230
What kind of plan?

1054
00:59:32,560 --> 00:59:33,560
Hm.

1055
00:59:39,490 --> 00:59:40,710
Not too shabby.

1056
00:59:40,950 --> 00:59:42,450
Way to come through, Sasuke.

1057
00:59:42,710 --> 00:59:45,130
Who wouldn't take their mask off in a hot
spring?

1058
00:59:45,430 --> 00:59:46,450
All right, you loser.

1059
00:59:46,690 --> 00:59:47,790
Zip your lip already.

1060
00:59:49,090 --> 00:59:50,090
Ah!

1061
00:59:50,370 --> 00:59:50,930
Hahahaha!

1062
00:59:50,931 --> 00:59:54,870
Tonight you breathe your last breath,
Kakashi.

1063
00:59:55,070 --> 00:59:58,664
I've coated this blow dart
with an elixir I concocted

1064
00:59:58,665 --> 01:00:01,530
that brings on wild and
uncontrollable laughter.

1065
01:00:03,450 --> 01:00:04,450
Hm?

1066
01:00:05,970 --> 01:00:06,970
Hahahaha!

1067
01:00:13,910 --> 01:00:15,930
You'll die laughing!

1068
01:00:16,430 --> 01:00:19,030
A fitting end for one such as you.

1069
01:00:19,770 --> 01:00:20,930
Oh, man.

1070
01:00:21,210 --> 01:00:22,790
I wanted to get a look, too.

1071
01:00:23,680 --> 01:00:25,790
But with these hot springs, I'm out of the
loop.

1072
01:00:26,025 --> 01:00:27,025
I wanna see.

1073
01:00:27,809 --> 01:00:28,809
Oh...

1074
01:00:29,870 --> 01:00:31,950
What's the holdup, Kakashi-sensei?

1075
01:00:32,070 --> 01:00:32,850
One sec.

1076
01:00:32,890 --> 01:00:33,590
I'm coming.

1077
01:00:33,890 --> 01:00:33,990
Hm?

1078
01:00:34,380 --> 01:00:35,850
I gotta see this.

1079
01:00:39,790 --> 01:00:40,790
This is it!

1080
01:00:40,910 --> 01:00:41,910
Here we go!

1081
01:00:42,090 --> 01:00:44,030
Oh, I can't see a thing!

1082
01:00:52,290 --> 01:00:53,290
Hm...

1083
01:00:57,370 --> 01:00:58,370
Phew!

1084
01:00:59,810 --> 01:01:04,691
It is hot in here... And I'm just
coming in for a minute... Ah!

1085
01:01:05,410 --> 01:01:07,090
You've gotta be kidding!

1086
01:01:07,390 --> 01:01:08,390
Hm?

1087
01:01:09,170 --> 01:01:12,430
What's up with you
two... Well, I'm getting in.

1088
01:01:16,730 --> 01:01:17,410
Ah...

1089
01:01:17,510 --> 01:01:18,510
Ahh.

1090
01:01:18,844 --> 01:01:19,844
Hahahaha!

1091
01:01:20,050 --> 01:01:20,730
Ah!

1092
01:01:20,790 --> 01:01:21,790
Ah!

1093
01:01:24,270 --> 01:01:26,110
You escaped again!

1094
01:01:26,750 --> 01:01:28,070
What's going on?

1095
01:01:28,250 --> 01:01:29,310
This is killing me!

1096
01:01:36,740 --> 01:01:37,530
Just great!

1097
01:01:37,670 --> 01:01:40,410
What the heck was Kakashi-sensei thinking
back there?

1098
01:01:40,411 --> 01:01:41,411
Huh?

1099
01:01:49,030 --> 01:01:52,130
Oh man, I'm completely flushed.

1100
01:01:53,654 --> 01:01:56,470
Where did our claws go?!

1101
01:02:05,130 --> 01:02:07,070
Come back anytime now!

1102
01:02:07,370 --> 01:02:08,110
Thank you very much!

1103
01:02:08,170 --> 01:02:09,030
Safe journey, Cam!

1104
01:02:09,190 --> 01:02:10,190
We'll come back anytime!

1105
01:02:10,410 --> 01:02:11,410
We'll come back anytime!

1106
01:02:13,270 --> 01:02:14,910
Curse you, Kakashi Hatake!

1107
01:02:15,210 --> 01:02:16,970
I will be your doom!

1108
01:02:17,330 --> 01:02:20,490
It's a good thing we brought along a spare
set of clothes, huh boss?

1109
01:02:21,430 --> 01:02:23,590
Yeah, I wonder who took them anyway?

1110
01:02:25,850 --> 01:02:28,610
Alright, you've all got jobs to do.

1111
01:02:28,750 --> 01:02:29,970
You'd best get to work.

1112
01:02:31,150 --> 01:02:32,150
Dismissed.

1113
01:02:32,990 --> 01:02:34,290
I'm about out of guys.

1114
01:02:34,590 --> 01:02:37,150
I don't think my nerves can handle much
more of this.

1115
01:02:37,750 --> 01:02:39,610
I'm getting pretty fed up myself.

1116
01:02:40,410 --> 01:02:41,530
Yeah, me too.

1117
01:02:41,830 --> 01:02:43,510
That makes three of us.

1118
01:02:43,910 --> 01:02:46,790
Alright then, desperate times call for
desperate measures!

1119
01:02:47,490 --> 01:02:48,490
Desperate measures?

1120
01:02:49,470 --> 01:02:51,490
Why are we dressed like this?

1121
01:02:51,730 --> 01:02:52,730
Isn't it obvious?

1122
01:02:52,965 --> 01:02:54,790
We're posing as a trio of rogue ninja!

1123
01:02:55,070 --> 01:02:56,650
Where did you even get these things?

1124
01:02:56,750 --> 01:02:59,190
Look, let's not get bogged down in the
details.

1125
01:02:59,390 --> 01:03:00,630
Do you even have a plan?

1126
01:03:02,230 --> 01:03:04,830
Strip off the mask, by force if we have
to!

1127
01:03:04,831 --> 01:03:05,831
Let's do it!

1128
01:03:11,084 --> 01:03:12,270
Alright, Kakashi.

1129
01:03:12,530 --> 01:03:13,530
Boss, look!

1130
01:03:16,420 --> 01:03:17,670
Hey, Kakashi Hatake!

1131
01:03:18,970 --> 01:03:19,450
Huh?

1132
01:03:19,750 --> 01:03:21,110
What are the three of you up to?

1133
01:03:21,290 --> 01:03:22,690
What are you talking about?

1134
01:03:23,070 --> 01:03:24,390
We're just three wandering ninja!

1135
01:03:24,570 --> 01:03:27,130
It's not like we want to see what's behind
your mask or anything!

1136
01:03:27,230 --> 01:03:27,890
You idiot!

1137
01:03:28,130 --> 01:03:29,850
Don't say any more than you have to!

1138
01:03:30,290 --> 01:03:31,290
That's my suit!

1139
01:03:31,450 --> 01:03:35,590
Hey boss, it looks like you're not the only
one who wants to get revenge on Kakashi.

1140
01:03:35,591 --> 01:03:36,830
Now's our chance!

1141
01:03:37,384 --> 01:03:38,570
Let's do it!

1142
01:03:38,790 --> 01:03:39,790
Right!

1143
01:03:40,190 --> 01:03:40,910
Hold it!

1144
01:03:40,990 --> 01:03:42,170
Right there!

1145
01:03:44,790 --> 01:03:47,730
Kakashi, it's time you pay for your
transgressions.

1146
01:03:48,210 --> 01:03:50,743
And the price is death,
delivered in the form of

1147
01:03:50,744 --> 01:03:53,411
this elixir, which will make
you weep uncontrollably!

1148
01:03:56,310 --> 01:03:57,130
That's funny.

1149
01:03:57,310 --> 01:04:00,250
I was just wondering how long you fellas
were going to hide for.

1150
01:04:00,470 --> 01:04:02,710
And you finally decide to show yourselves.

1151
01:04:05,590 --> 01:04:06,790
First things first, though.

1152
01:04:06,830 --> 01:04:08,450
Sasuke, Sakura, Naruto...

1153
01:04:09,610 --> 01:04:11,810
Why on earth are you dressed like that?

1154
01:04:12,330 --> 01:04:12,670
Huh?

1155
01:04:12,910 --> 01:04:16,171
Uh, well, the
thing is... Oh boy!

1156
01:04:16,270 --> 01:04:18,190
We'd better come up with something fast!

1157
01:04:18,790 --> 01:04:19,830
You fools!

1158
01:04:20,110 --> 01:04:21,610
You fell right into our trap!

1159
01:04:21,810 --> 01:04:24,710
We've known all along you were targeting
Kakashi-sensei!

1160
01:04:24,990 --> 01:04:25,990
That's impossible!

1161
01:04:26,490 --> 01:04:30,270
Are you telling me that our machinations
were exposed from the very beginning?

1162
01:04:30,670 --> 01:04:31,710
Of course!

1163
01:04:31,930 --> 01:04:35,570
This was all just a ruse to lure you guys
out, and you fell for it!

1164
01:04:35,571 --> 01:04:36,730
Hook, line, and sinker!

1165
01:04:36,810 --> 01:04:38,910
So we were caught up in your web of
deception!

1166
01:04:39,450 --> 01:04:39,770
Crash!

1167
01:04:39,870 --> 01:04:42,170
We underestimated them because they were
kids!

1168
01:04:42,750 --> 01:04:44,990
No one filled me in on any of this.

1169
01:04:45,150 --> 01:04:46,330
Nice work, Sakura.

1170
01:04:46,690 --> 01:04:51,110
Well, I'm not sure I really get what's
going on around here, but... whatever.

1171
01:04:54,990 --> 01:04:56,170
Please forgive us!

1172
01:04:56,250 --> 01:04:57,250
Forgive us!

1173
01:04:57,690 --> 01:04:59,750
Words aren't going to help you,
kid.

1174
01:05:09,250 --> 01:05:11,850
This is just like three years ago all over
again!

1175
01:05:11,970 --> 01:05:14,430
We're swinging from a rope like an
oversized yo-yo!

1176
01:05:14,570 --> 01:05:16,650
You've got us all trussed up in the same
stupid rope!

1177
01:05:16,651 --> 01:05:19,330
Hey, by the way, who are you guys?

1178
01:05:19,530 --> 01:05:21,550
And he doesn't even remember who we are!

1179
01:05:29,110 --> 01:05:30,670
Hey, Kakashi-sensei!

1180
01:05:30,810 --> 01:05:31,810
Yeah?

1181
01:05:32,050 --> 01:05:33,570
What are you hiding under that mask?

1182
01:05:34,850 --> 01:05:35,850
What?

1183
01:05:35,890 --> 01:05:37,590
You want to know what's behind my mask?

1184
01:05:37,770 --> 01:05:37,910
Yeah!

1185
01:05:38,270 --> 01:05:40,510
You should have just said so in the first
place.

1186
01:05:41,110 --> 01:05:42,490
So does that mean you'll show us?

1187
01:05:43,160 --> 01:05:44,160
Sure, I don't mind.

1188
01:05:45,660 --> 01:05:46,660
What's the big deal?

1189
01:05:50,210 --> 01:05:51,210
Alright.

1190
01:05:54,990 --> 01:05:56,350
Is it limp lips?

1191
01:05:59,330 --> 01:06:00,610
Or buck teeth?

1192
01:06:03,130 --> 01:06:05,530
Or a tiny mouth?

1193
01:06:05,950 --> 01:06:11,090
Behind this mask...
Behind that mask...

1194
01:06:12,170 --> 01:06:13,930
...is another mask!

1195
01:06:14,430 --> 01:06:15,430
Pretty cool, huh?

1196
01:06:20,250 --> 01:06:22,850
Are you freaking kidding me?

1197
01:06:22,990 --> 01:06:24,910
What the hell kind of ending is that?

1198
01:06:31,590 --> 01:06:34,490
We've received intel on the thieves who
took the golden statue.

1199
01:06:35,070 --> 01:06:37,750
They're either on land on this forest
path...

1200
01:06:37,751 --> 01:06:41,430
...or they're sailing by boat and will
land somewhere in this area.

1201
01:06:43,580 --> 01:06:47,490
So, we'll split into two teams and wait
for them in both locations.

1202
01:06:48,340 --> 01:06:53,791
Now, to keep the teams balanced, I'll be
on one and you three will be on the other.

1203
01:06:54,070 --> 01:06:55,690
Hold on, what does that mean?

1204
01:06:55,910 --> 01:06:59,090
Are you saying that Sasuke needs all the
help he can get?

1205
01:06:59,091 --> 01:07:00,490
No, he means you.

1206
01:07:01,030 --> 01:07:05,470
I know I'm not up to your level yet,
but I doubt you need three on one team.

1207
01:07:05,910 --> 01:07:08,250
So, why don't you take Naruto off my
hands?

1208
01:07:08,410 --> 01:07:11,030
You subtract his skill from yours and
we'll be even.

1209
01:07:12,830 --> 01:07:16,890
Sasuke, is this just a clever ruse so that
you and I can be alone together?

1210
01:07:20,130 --> 01:07:22,130
Come on, you've got to be kidding!

1211
01:07:22,470 --> 01:07:24,710
Why would my skill subtract from his?

1212
01:07:24,930 --> 01:07:26,870
Simple, because you have nothing to add.

1213
01:07:27,090 --> 01:07:28,090
What?

1214
01:07:28,810 --> 01:07:31,670
Sasuke wants to be with me so much he
can't even breathe!

1215
01:07:31,730 --> 01:07:33,370
You're as annoying as he is.

1216
01:07:40,540 --> 01:07:41,540
Pay attention now.

1217
01:07:43,340 --> 01:07:47,110
I'll watch the pier and you three will
keep an eye on this path in the forest.

1218
01:07:48,210 --> 01:07:51,210
If the thieves appear, notify me right
away.

1219
01:07:51,430 --> 01:07:53,090
Do not underestimate them.

1220
01:07:53,410 --> 01:07:56,150
Our mission is to retrieve a stolen golden
statue.

1221
01:07:56,151 --> 01:07:58,930
We must proceed with the utmost caution.

1222
01:08:00,470 --> 01:08:04,330
If the thieves appear at my location,
I'll send a signal with this.

1223
01:08:05,044 --> 01:08:09,190
When this lightning barrel is tossed into
the air, it'll release a thunderbolt.

1224
01:08:09,590 --> 01:08:13,430
Once you verify that it went off, rush
straight to the location that it marks.

1225
01:08:13,770 --> 01:08:15,430
You better be careful with that.

1226
01:08:15,550 --> 01:08:17,069
I don't want to get zapped again.

1227
01:08:17,630 --> 01:08:20,630
Remember, you three are not to act on your
own.

1228
01:08:21,770 --> 01:08:22,770
Hmm...

1229
01:08:30,859 --> 01:08:32,200
It's the thieves!

1230
01:08:48,560 --> 01:08:49,920
You idiot!

1231
01:08:50,319 --> 01:08:52,640
Be careful with that treasure,
you hear me?

1232
01:08:53,020 --> 01:08:55,120
Yes, sorry, Boss Jaco!

1233
01:08:55,260 --> 01:08:56,260
Get it together!

1234
01:08:56,580 --> 01:08:57,580
Yes, sir!

1235
01:08:58,020 --> 01:08:59,899
The treasure's in that wicker box?

1236
01:09:00,960 --> 01:09:01,740
This is it.

1237
01:09:01,760 --> 01:09:03,500
This is my big chance!

1238
01:09:05,220 --> 01:09:06,920
You're amazing, Naruto!

1239
01:09:07,220 --> 01:09:09,120
You're so much cooler than Sasuke!

1240
01:09:09,319 --> 01:09:10,620
You really showed him up!

1241
01:09:14,220 --> 01:09:14,520
Huh?

1242
01:09:15,150 --> 01:09:17,399
Don't tell me he's planning the same
thing.

1243
01:09:19,090 --> 01:09:20,779
I'm not gonna lose to him!

1244
01:09:27,540 --> 01:09:28,540
What?

1245
01:09:29,000 --> 01:09:30,460
What is this?

1246
01:09:33,500 --> 01:09:34,500
Huh?

1247
01:09:40,200 --> 01:09:41,560
Damn it!

1248
01:09:41,680 --> 01:09:42,880
They took the treasure!

1249
01:09:43,240 --> 01:09:44,436
What do they think they're doing?

1250
01:09:44,460 --> 01:09:46,920
We're supposed to notify Kakashi-sensei
first!

1251
01:09:49,120 --> 01:09:50,460
There's another one!

1252
01:10:11,960 --> 01:10:14,460
You two, give me that treasure back!

1253
01:10:14,740 --> 01:10:15,520
No way!

1254
01:10:15,660 --> 01:10:16,660
Forget it!

1255
01:10:16,720 --> 01:10:17,820
Then take this!

1256
01:10:20,340 --> 01:10:21,340
Ah!

1257
01:10:30,560 --> 01:10:32,500
I'm not gonna lose it now!

1258
01:10:32,880 --> 01:10:33,880
Ah!

1259
01:10:36,140 --> 01:10:37,140
Ah!

1260
01:10:38,700 --> 01:10:39,700
Ah!

1261
01:10:39,820 --> 01:10:40,500
Ah!

1262
01:10:40,560 --> 01:10:41,240
Ah!

1263
01:10:41,241 --> 01:10:42,241
Ah!

1264
01:10:48,960 --> 01:10:49,960
Damn!

1265
01:10:58,420 --> 01:11:00,660
So the Hidden Leaf's coming after us,
huh?

1266
01:11:01,700 --> 01:11:03,780
Were those two the only ones with you?

1267
01:11:07,200 --> 01:11:09,600
I know that there must be more of you.

1268
01:11:10,120 --> 01:11:13,900
Yeah, that's why you tried to send that
signal to reveal our location.

1269
01:11:27,220 --> 01:11:28,740
It's pretty cool, isn't it?

1270
01:11:28,960 --> 01:11:32,820
Clearly, I'm a natural-born thief who's
rotten to the very core of this being.

1271
01:11:33,020 --> 01:11:38,361
So rotten, in fact, that as you can clearly
see, even my chakra has become new fowl.

1272
01:11:40,520 --> 01:11:42,800
Those two Frenzivers escaped downstream.

1273
01:11:43,540 --> 01:11:46,062
We'll split up and
search the river until we

1274
01:11:46,063 --> 01:11:48,380
find them, and then we'll
take back our treasure.

1275
01:11:48,700 --> 01:11:50,140
What do we do with her?

1276
01:11:50,520 --> 01:11:53,300
We'll bring her with us and keep her as a
hostage.

1277
01:12:00,620 --> 01:12:05,740
I can't believe they stole something as
ridiculous as this... this... teddy bear.

1278
01:12:06,100 --> 01:12:08,520
The thunderbolt.

1279
01:12:09,760 --> 01:12:11,480
The signal to warn Kakashi.

1280
01:12:12,060 --> 01:12:13,560
It didn't go off, did it?

1281
01:12:13,760 --> 01:12:15,120
Oh... no.

1282
01:12:15,121 --> 01:12:17,920
Maybe... Sakura couldn't release it.

1283
01:12:18,760 --> 01:12:21,160
You think Sakura... was captured?

1284
01:12:25,880 --> 01:12:26,880
What?

1285
01:12:28,780 --> 01:12:29,320
What?

1286
01:12:29,380 --> 01:12:31,180
What is this?

1287
01:12:31,960 --> 01:12:32,960
What?

1288
01:12:33,100 --> 01:12:34,640
What's going on?

1289
01:12:34,980 --> 01:12:36,260
We're stuck together.

1290
01:12:40,780 --> 01:12:41,780
Ready?

1291
01:12:41,860 --> 01:12:42,860
Pull!

1292
01:12:45,120 --> 01:12:46,120
Here we come!

1293
01:12:48,620 --> 01:12:50,020
Take this!

1294
01:12:50,021 --> 01:12:51,021
And...

1295
01:12:52,880 --> 01:12:56,120
And... And...

1296
01:12:58,000 --> 01:13:01,440
And... ... oh.

1297
01:13:58,490 --> 01:14:00,810
Why do I always end up kissing you?

1298
01:14:01,150 --> 01:14:03,450
You took the words right out of my mouth!

1299
01:14:16,180 --> 01:14:18,920
Don't worry, you'll see your friends soon
enough.

1300
01:14:19,800 --> 01:14:22,397
After they return the
treasure, I'll make sure that

1301
01:14:22,398 --> 01:14:25,120
you're all back together
again in the afterlife.

1302
01:14:27,120 --> 01:14:31,580
You're ninja, but even ninja become
helpless if their hands are bound.

1303
01:14:35,640 --> 01:14:39,380
Sasuke... Naruto... Sakura...

1304
01:14:41,460 --> 01:14:46,261
While we're stuck like this,
Sakura could be... Naruto!

1305
01:14:47,760 --> 01:14:48,980
Stop, you idiot!

1306
01:14:49,400 --> 01:14:50,560
Hang tight, Sakura!

1307
01:14:51,120 --> 01:14:52,900
I'm coming to save you right now!

1308
01:14:53,500 --> 01:14:55,040
Listen, just wait, you loser!

1309
01:14:59,980 --> 01:15:02,040
Just what the hell are you doing,
Sasuke?

1310
01:15:02,360 --> 01:15:05,520
I mean, don't you even care what happens
to Sakura?

1311
01:15:05,760 --> 01:15:07,080
Look, we will save her.

1312
01:15:07,160 --> 01:15:09,360
But we can't do anything when we're like
this.

1313
01:15:09,380 --> 01:15:13,280
Saving her no matter what stands in the
way is what a true friend would do!

1314
01:15:14,220 --> 01:15:19,060
I just... I don't want people to say that
I'm scum!

1315
01:15:19,460 --> 01:15:21,620
Who doesn't care about his friends!

1316
01:15:22,900 --> 01:15:27,280
Those ninja who abandon their friends are
even worse than scum.

1317
01:15:27,940 --> 01:15:28,940
Yeah, fine!

1318
01:15:29,160 --> 01:15:31,760
But joining up with Kakashi is still the
right move!

1319
01:15:32,020 --> 01:15:33,940
It'll increase her chances of survival!

1320
01:15:34,840 --> 01:15:37,000
Look, don't talk to me about her chances!

1321
01:15:37,001 --> 01:15:40,080
That just depends on how hard we work to
save her!

1322
01:15:40,720 --> 01:15:43,940
There's no way I'll let her die over this
stupid thing!

1323
01:15:44,200 --> 01:15:45,200
You idiot!

1324
01:15:45,340 --> 01:15:46,660
Naruto, stop it!

1325
01:15:49,620 --> 01:15:50,820
No, dammit!

1326
01:15:51,180 --> 01:15:52,180
Dammit!

1327
01:15:52,360 --> 01:15:53,360
Dammit!

1328
01:15:53,540 --> 01:15:54,540
Dammit!

1329
01:15:56,380 --> 01:16:01,080
But... someone who doesn't take his
mission seriously is scum too.

1330
01:16:03,320 --> 01:16:04,320
Yeah...

1331
01:16:08,930 --> 01:16:09,930
Gotta be.

1332
01:16:10,190 --> 01:16:11,190
You... what?

1333
01:16:11,695 --> 01:16:12,695
I said...

1334
01:16:13,360 --> 01:16:14,670
I gotta go take a leak!

1335
01:16:17,650 --> 01:16:19,230
Hey, what in the hell?

1336
01:16:19,550 --> 01:16:21,550
Oh, uh, okay, one-handed then.

1337
01:16:21,750 --> 01:16:22,750
What?

1338
01:16:22,830 --> 01:16:23,830
Cut it out!

1339
01:16:23,870 --> 01:16:24,910
Not so close!

1340
01:16:25,265 --> 01:16:26,425
You're gonna splash it on me!

1341
01:16:26,780 --> 01:16:29,490
Listen, I'm sorry, but if you gotta go,
you gotta go!

1342
01:16:29,850 --> 01:16:30,850
Just hold it!

1343
01:16:31,070 --> 01:16:32,070
I can't!

1344
01:16:32,810 --> 01:16:33,810
Knock it off!

1345
01:16:33,910 --> 01:16:34,570
Stop it!

1346
01:16:34,610 --> 01:16:35,610
Zip it up!

1347
01:16:35,690 --> 01:16:36,690
Huh?

1348
01:16:41,700 --> 01:16:42,700
Ah!

1349
01:16:53,440 --> 01:16:55,100
Don't get in my way, Naruto!

1350
01:16:55,700 --> 01:16:56,780
Are you kidding?

1351
01:16:56,980 --> 01:16:58,280
You're the one who's in my way!

1352
01:16:59,600 --> 01:17:00,200
Stop!

1353
01:17:00,540 --> 01:17:02,140
Give us back the treasure!

1354
01:17:07,460 --> 01:17:09,360
Multi-Shadow Clone Jutsu!

1355
01:17:13,080 --> 01:17:15,160
You can't weave a sign like this,
idiot!

1356
01:17:15,320 --> 01:17:16,320
You need two hands!

1357
01:17:16,560 --> 01:17:20,740
It's like I said before, we don't have a
chance, even if they are weaker than we are!

1358
01:17:20,900 --> 01:17:21,900
I know that now!

1359
01:17:31,370 --> 01:17:31,830
Naruto!

1360
01:17:31,831 --> 01:17:32,831
Stop this!

1361
01:17:32,870 --> 01:17:33,150
No!

1362
01:17:33,370 --> 01:17:34,370
No way!

1363
01:17:35,090 --> 01:17:37,770
If you're not in, I'll cut my arm off,
then go!

1364
01:17:39,570 --> 01:17:40,870
I'm gonna beat this guy!

1365
01:17:41,070 --> 01:17:42,690
And then go and save Sakura!

1366
01:17:42,691 --> 01:17:43,691
Sakura!

1367
01:17:50,910 --> 01:17:52,490
You're always so reckless!

1368
01:18:02,710 --> 01:18:03,850
Alright, let's go!

1369
01:18:04,530 --> 01:18:05,570
Time to save Sakura!

1370
01:18:06,860 --> 01:18:08,876
If those guys came
this far, they'll probably

1371
01:18:08,877 --> 01:18:11,191
find us before we can
meet Kakashi-sensei.

1372
01:18:11,700 --> 01:18:14,307
If that's the case, it'll
be faster if we just make

1373
01:18:14,308 --> 01:18:16,990
this guy tell us where
Sakura is and save her first.

1374
01:18:17,270 --> 01:18:18,270
Huh?

1375
01:18:18,330 --> 01:18:18,870
Sasuke...

1376
01:18:19,270 --> 01:18:22,710
However, to succeed, we have to work
together perfectly.

1377
01:18:23,350 --> 01:18:24,350
Huh?

1378
01:18:24,590 --> 01:18:25,590
Got it!

1379
01:18:28,350 --> 01:18:29,350
I just remembered.

1380
01:18:30,280 --> 01:18:31,280
I gotta pee.

1381
01:18:38,130 --> 01:18:39,730
I just remembered.

1382
01:18:39,730 --> 01:18:39,730
I gotta pee.

1383
01:18:39,731 --> 01:18:40,731
Me too.

1384
01:18:44,969 --> 01:18:45,969
What

1385
01:18:57,670 --> 01:19:00,900
do you mean, Sugoro still hasn't reported
back yet?

1386
01:19:01,350 --> 01:19:03,300
You know, I wonder...

1387
01:19:03,575 --> 01:19:04,660
You're wondering right!

1388
01:19:04,900 --> 01:19:05,900
We got him!

1389
01:19:07,560 --> 01:19:08,360
Sasuke!

1390
01:19:08,520 --> 01:19:09,520
Naruto!

1391
01:19:11,200 --> 01:19:12,000
Sasuke!

1392
01:19:12,000 --> 01:19:12,000
Naruto!

1393
01:19:12,700 --> 01:19:13,700
There!

1394
01:19:21,030 --> 01:19:21,590
Hah!

1395
01:19:21,830 --> 01:19:22,590
That's right!

1396
01:19:22,770 --> 01:19:24,370
We're back and free at last!

1397
01:19:24,865 --> 01:19:28,330
Only a feudal lord's sister would own a
statue like that one.

1398
01:19:28,900 --> 01:19:31,430
And that's exactly what managed to pull us
apart.

1399
01:19:31,905 --> 01:19:33,690
So their hands are free now?

1400
01:19:34,769 --> 01:19:35,990
Here's our offer.

1401
01:19:36,410 --> 01:19:39,630
We'll let you have this back, in exchange
for our teammate.

1402
01:19:40,110 --> 01:19:42,370
Refuse and I'll pulverize every one of
you!

1403
01:19:42,371 --> 01:19:45,910
Trust me, that won't be a problem now that
my hands are free!

1404
01:19:57,120 --> 01:19:58,360
We're both ninja.

1405
01:19:58,900 --> 01:20:01,820
Surely you don't think mere robbers can
defeat us.

1406
01:20:02,060 --> 01:20:03,300
You can't.

1407
01:20:22,770 --> 01:20:23,770
Huh.

1408
01:20:23,950 --> 01:20:26,730
Tell me, why are you gritting your teeth
so hard?

1409
01:20:28,990 --> 01:20:30,050
You're sweating.

1410
01:20:30,190 --> 01:20:32,710
Your veins are practically popping out of
your skin.

1411
01:20:35,470 --> 01:20:36,510
Alright then.

1412
01:20:36,850 --> 01:20:39,430
If you're truly free, then come over here!

1413
01:20:40,410 --> 01:20:41,410
Come on!

1414
01:20:45,780 --> 01:20:46,820
Just as I thought.

1415
01:20:47,100 --> 01:20:48,580
Their hands are still fused.

1416
01:20:48,880 --> 01:20:49,880
There's nothing to fear.

1417
01:20:50,200 --> 01:20:51,200
Get him!

1418
01:20:53,320 --> 01:20:54,860
He called our bluff.

1419
01:20:55,180 --> 01:20:56,400
Then we have no choice.

1420
01:20:57,020 --> 01:21:01,900
Are you?

1421
01:21:06,340 --> 01:21:07,340
Naruto!

1422
01:21:10,300 --> 01:21:11,300
Right!

1423
01:21:23,060 --> 01:21:27,980
locked up.urd.

1424
01:21:33,720 --> 01:21:36,500
...Where, brother?

1425
01:21:36,860 --> 01:21:37,880
It means... They've within.

1426
01:21:38,860 --> 01:21:40,720
Lucky they're alive!

1427
01:21:46,600 --> 01:21:49,780
Can't change people in I just can't!

1428
01:22:00,540 --> 01:22:02,480
Even like this, we can take that guy.

1429
01:22:03,060 --> 01:22:04,060
Let's go!

1430
01:22:28,880 --> 01:22:30,620
Don't even think about it!

1431
01:22:37,020 --> 01:22:38,020
Fire style!

1432
01:22:38,600 --> 01:22:39,800
Shadowpaw jutsu!

1433
01:22:40,620 --> 01:22:41,620
No way!

1434
01:22:41,800 --> 01:22:42,800
A hand sign!

1435
01:22:43,720 --> 01:22:44,720
No.

1436
01:22:45,000 --> 01:22:49,140
Even if we could weave signs, we couldn't
infuse chakra like this, idiot.

1437
01:22:49,500 --> 01:22:51,160
Don't treat me like a fool!

1438
01:22:52,080 --> 01:22:54,220
But we do have a combination attack!

1439
01:22:54,580 --> 01:22:55,580
You what?

1440
01:22:55,720 --> 01:22:56,780
Pachinko jutsu!

1441
01:23:00,660 --> 01:23:01,660
Well,

1442
01:23:13,960 --> 01:23:16,540
maybe it can be melted down and recast.

1443
01:23:16,770 --> 01:23:18,560
Though that's a pretty big maybe.

1444
01:23:18,860 --> 01:23:20,820
Oh Sasuke, thank you!

1445
01:23:21,340 --> 01:23:21,500
What?

1446
01:23:22,060 --> 01:23:24,780
He didn't do it by himself, you know,
Sakura.

1447
01:23:25,200 --> 01:23:26,560
This is getting ridiculous!

1448
01:23:26,940 --> 01:23:29,080
Can't you do anything, Kakashi-sensei?

1449
01:23:29,460 --> 01:23:31,860
Look, that thief already told you guys.

1450
01:23:32,140 --> 01:23:35,040
It'll just crumble apart on its own in two
or three days.

1451
01:23:35,360 --> 01:23:38,140
If I have to put up with him that long,
I'll kill him!

1452
01:23:38,200 --> 01:23:40,180
I should be the one who's saying that!

1453
01:23:42,620 --> 01:23:43,660
Uh-oh.

1454
01:23:44,400 --> 01:23:45,400
I gotta go.

1455
01:23:46,200 --> 01:23:47,200
Again?

1456
01:23:47,380 --> 01:23:48,380
Yes, again.

1457
01:23:49,120 --> 01:23:50,880
And this time it's number two.

1458
01:23:51,700 --> 01:23:53,200
You gotta be kidding me!

1459
01:23:54,100 --> 01:23:55,680
Don't you dare, Naruto!

1460
01:23:56,680 --> 01:23:59,480
Come on, we already peed together,
what's the big deal?

1461
01:23:59,960 --> 01:24:01,700
This is so much worse!

1462
01:24:06,300 --> 01:24:10,080
Those who abandon their friends are worse
than scum.

1463
01:24:11,340 --> 01:24:14,440
These three overcome their differences so
easily.

1464
01:24:16,780 --> 01:24:17,780
Hm.

1465
01:24:39,740 --> 01:24:45,060
Okay... Alright, with that being said, our
mission is now over-we're all dismissed.

1466
01:24:45,440 --> 01:24:45,760
Already?

1467
01:24:46,080 --> 01:24:47,360
It's only 10 in the morning!

1468
01:24:47,580 --> 01:24:49,200
Our missions have been so boring!

1469
01:24:49,500 --> 01:24:52,280
When we gonna get an S rank mission,
come on?

1470
01:24:52,560 --> 01:24:52,680
Hm.

1471
01:24:52,780 --> 01:24:53,420
S rank?

1472
01:24:53,680 --> 01:24:55,680
Yeah right, a loser like you?

1473
01:24:55,840 --> 01:24:56,880
What you talking about?

1474
01:24:57,200 --> 01:24:57,580
H Yuko?

1475
01:24:57,581 --> 01:24:58,660
We're slip only Ganon.

1476
01:24:58,660 --> 01:24:58,660
H Yuko?

1477
01:24:58,661 --> 01:24:59,140
I mean, remember?

1478
01:24:59,560 --> 01:25:02,920
I want something with more pizzazz,
more oomph, so...

1479
01:25:03,095 --> 01:25:04,520
There just aren't any missions.

1480
01:25:04,860 --> 01:25:05,900
Anyway, dismissed.

1481
01:25:07,485 --> 01:25:08,940
You heard him!

1482
01:25:09,080 --> 01:25:12,340
So, Sasuke, how about today,
the two of us... I'm going home.

1483
01:25:12,724 --> 01:25:14,660
Wait, just hold on a minute.

1484
01:25:14,820 --> 01:25:18,680
I know a 1S-rank mission the three of us
could actually do right now.

1485
01:25:19,060 --> 01:25:21,860
A mission that's failed again and again.

1486
01:25:22,020 --> 01:25:23,920
One that only we can pull off.

1487
01:25:25,050 --> 01:25:28,100
To see what Kakashi-sensei's face really
looks like.

1488
01:25:28,660 --> 01:25:31,300
Let's find out our target's best-kept
secret!

1489
01:25:32,315 --> 01:25:34,360
Do you even know what you're saying?

1490
01:25:36,540 --> 01:25:38,280
Listen, just forget about that.

1491
01:25:38,380 --> 01:25:39,380
It's impossible.

1492
01:25:39,935 --> 01:25:41,420
I mean, right, Sasuke?

1493
01:25:41,640 --> 01:25:44,180
This would be the perfect mission for a
day like today.

1494
01:25:44,480 --> 01:25:45,640
I couldn't agree more.

1495
01:25:46,800 --> 01:25:47,320
Sasuke!

1496
01:25:47,520 --> 01:25:48,460
How could you?

1497
01:25:48,500 --> 01:25:49,500
You betrayed me!

1498
01:25:51,900 --> 01:25:53,440
But what do we do?

1499
01:25:53,580 --> 01:25:56,280
Every single time we try this,
it never goes well.

1500
01:25:57,160 --> 01:25:58,160
Not to worry.

1501
01:25:58,660 --> 01:25:59,660
I already have a plan!

1502
01:26:00,140 --> 01:26:01,220
What is it?

1503
01:26:02,280 --> 01:26:02,800
Photographs!

1504
01:26:02,801 --> 01:26:05,567
If we go through every
single photo Kakashi-sensei is

1505
01:26:05,568 --> 01:26:08,120
in, there's bound to be at
least one without a mask!

1506
01:26:08,320 --> 01:26:12,620
Actually, I never told you this, but I
already checked them out once before.

1507
01:26:13,300 --> 01:26:15,420
And he has a mask on in every one!

1508
01:26:15,820 --> 01:26:19,360
The photo submitted to the Hokage for the
ninja registration form.

1509
01:26:20,150 --> 01:26:23,460
That should be a picture of him where he
isn't wearing a mask.

1510
01:26:24,015 --> 01:26:27,460
But of course, it's an extremely
classified top-secret document.

1511
01:26:27,461 --> 01:26:30,400
Getting your hands on it won't be an easy
task.

1512
01:26:30,780 --> 01:26:31,920
Who are you?

1513
01:26:32,935 --> 01:26:33,680
I'm Sakeya.

1514
01:26:33,880 --> 01:26:34,880
I'm a photographer.

1515
01:26:35,470 --> 01:26:38,020
I travel from east to west looking for
stories.

1516
01:26:38,100 --> 01:26:39,100
Not north or south!

1517
01:26:39,700 --> 01:26:43,260
Naruto, stop getting hung up on
insignificant details!

1518
01:26:43,570 --> 01:26:46,081
Well, anyway, I was on
the hunt for a scoop, and I

1519
01:26:46,082 --> 01:26:48,400
happened to overhear
your fascinating conversation.

1520
01:26:48,680 --> 01:26:49,660
He did hear us!

1521
01:26:49,680 --> 01:26:50,580
Let's get rid of him!

1522
01:26:50,680 --> 01:26:51,680
Ready?

1523
01:26:51,974 --> 01:26:52,974
Idiot!

1524
01:26:53,060 --> 01:26:55,740
This guy's right.

1525
01:26:56,670 --> 01:26:57,670
That is the regulation.

1526
01:26:58,190 --> 01:27:00,960
The ninja registration form photo must
show your face.

1527
01:27:01,720 --> 01:27:05,360
It's so obvious, but none of us even
thought about looking there before now.

1528
01:27:06,050 --> 01:27:07,774
So listen, do you think
you guys would let me

1529
01:27:07,775 --> 01:27:10,401
tag along with you
on this little adventure?

1530
01:27:10,570 --> 01:27:12,040
And why would you want to do that?

1531
01:27:12,640 --> 01:27:13,640
It's simple.

1532
01:27:13,840 --> 01:27:16,682
If I'm able to capture this
Kakashi guy without a mask on,

1533
01:27:16,683 --> 01:27:19,220
it'll be the biggest scoop
since the Leaf was established.

1534
01:27:20,270 --> 01:27:24,100
Even if it were to get hushed up, I'd
be sure to make a lot of money on this.

1535
01:27:24,320 --> 01:27:24,500
Oh!

1536
01:27:24,560 --> 01:27:24,880
Hey!

1537
01:27:24,980 --> 01:27:25,180
Hey!

1538
01:27:25,240 --> 01:27:25,660
Hold on!

1539
01:27:25,965 --> 01:27:28,365
When you get the money, you gotta treat us
to ramen, promise?

1540
01:27:28,890 --> 01:27:30,260
I'll even throw in some gyoza.

1541
01:27:30,530 --> 01:27:31,530
Does that sound good?

1542
01:27:31,680 --> 01:27:31,980
Hm.

1543
01:27:32,600 --> 01:27:33,900
Now this is getting interesting.

1544
01:27:36,260 --> 01:27:37,860
I don't know, you guys.

1545
01:27:38,640 --> 01:27:39,640
Aw, yeah!

1546
01:27:39,760 --> 01:27:41,180
I'm getting excited about this!

1547
01:27:50,520 --> 01:27:52,920
This is where they store secret documents.

1548
01:27:53,975 --> 01:27:55,700
This'll be an infiltration mission.

1549
01:27:57,220 --> 01:27:59,500
Sukeya, you think you'll be able to keep
up?

1550
01:28:00,310 --> 01:28:01,680
I don't think it'll be a problem.

1551
01:28:01,681 --> 01:28:04,760
Before I became a photographer,
I was a rank-and-file ninja.

1552
01:28:05,525 --> 01:28:06,525
All right.

1553
01:28:06,800 --> 01:28:08,300
Let's get this mission started.

1554
01:28:24,410 --> 01:28:26,010
You're still not done, Sasuke?

1555
01:28:26,190 --> 01:28:26,550
Shut up.

1556
01:28:26,570 --> 01:28:27,210
Just hold on.

1557
01:28:27,530 --> 01:28:28,750
Can we switch places?

1558
01:28:28,790 --> 01:28:29,790
Just for a moment.

1559
01:28:37,650 --> 01:28:38,650
Wow!

1560
01:28:39,070 --> 01:28:39,590
It opened!

1561
01:28:39,850 --> 01:28:40,850
That's awesome!

1562
01:28:40,930 --> 01:28:41,930
So, Sukeya.

1563
01:28:42,305 --> 01:28:44,430
What division did you belong to before?

1564
01:28:44,431 --> 01:28:46,610
Oh, I was in the intel unit.

1565
01:28:46,750 --> 01:28:48,490
That reported to Lord Hokage.

1566
01:28:49,010 --> 01:28:51,150
Wait, he means the... Anbu.

1567
01:28:51,290 --> 01:28:52,070
Black Ops.

1568
01:28:52,230 --> 01:28:53,230
Eh?

1569
01:28:53,355 --> 01:28:55,950
Well, something's happened, and now I'm
retired.

1570
01:28:56,430 --> 01:28:59,450
Given your past, is it wise for you to be
doing this?

1571
01:29:00,430 --> 01:29:02,330
You'll be targeted by the Anbu.

1572
01:29:03,270 --> 01:29:04,430
Don't worry about it.

1573
01:29:04,470 --> 01:29:05,470
I'll be just fine.

1574
01:29:05,550 --> 01:29:06,130
Come on.

1575
01:29:06,210 --> 01:29:07,210
Let's go.

1576
01:29:12,390 --> 01:29:14,310
We have to search all these?

1577
01:29:14,311 --> 01:29:15,311
Let's hurry.

1578
01:29:28,980 --> 01:29:29,860
Found it.

1579
01:29:29,960 --> 01:29:30,960
This is it.

1580
01:29:34,820 --> 01:29:35,680
All right.

1581
01:29:35,740 --> 01:29:36,740
Let's open it up.

1582
01:29:40,044 --> 01:29:41,060
No way!

1583
01:29:41,200 --> 01:29:42,640
The moment is finally here!

1584
01:29:55,960 --> 01:29:56,960
Don't move.

1585
01:29:59,620 --> 01:30:00,680
We're taking you in.

1586
01:30:01,235 --> 01:30:03,080
Make a move and we'll assume you're
resisting.

1587
01:30:03,790 --> 01:30:05,540
And we may have to take you down.

1588
01:30:05,620 --> 01:30:06,640
Uh-oh.

1589
01:30:06,720 --> 01:30:08,900
I feel like I'm gonna sneeze.

1590
01:30:09,360 --> 01:30:09,920
Idiot.

1591
01:30:09,921 --> 01:30:10,921
Hold it in.

1592
01:30:11,820 --> 01:30:12,820
Damn it.

1593
01:30:13,040 --> 01:30:14,380
And we were so close, too.

1594
01:30:27,719 --> 01:30:28,380
Really.

1595
01:30:28,680 --> 01:30:30,100
An infiltration mission.

1596
01:30:30,360 --> 01:30:30,860
I know.

1597
01:30:31,180 --> 01:30:32,780
I'm really sorry about that.

1598
01:30:32,840 --> 01:30:35,100
I tried to stop them, but they insisted on
doing it.

1599
01:30:35,101 --> 01:30:35,300
What?

1600
01:30:35,440 --> 01:30:36,280
You jerk!

1601
01:30:36,460 --> 01:30:39,600
So right from the start, you planned on
blaming us if this failed.

1602
01:30:40,225 --> 01:30:42,880
They just wanted to see what your face
really looked like.

1603
01:30:43,300 --> 01:30:45,500
You're a former Anbu black ops,
right?

1604
01:30:46,225 --> 01:30:47,700
Honestly, it's ridiculous.

1605
01:30:48,140 --> 01:30:50,980
Who cares what I look like underneath this
mask anyway?

1606
01:30:58,200 --> 01:31:00,520
You've really got some nerve blaming us!

1607
01:31:01,120 --> 01:31:04,220
I thought it was pretty strange that you
wanted to join us.

1608
01:31:04,221 --> 01:31:08,080
You're skilled and a former Anbu,
so you could have easily done this alone.

1609
01:31:08,340 --> 01:31:11,580
I can't stand handsome guys who think they
can get away with awful things.

1610
01:31:11,940 --> 01:31:12,940
Sorry, sorry.

1611
01:31:13,260 --> 01:31:16,500
How about I make it up to you by helping
you photograph Kakashi's face?

1612
01:31:17,180 --> 01:31:19,360
Take advantage of my photography skills.

1613
01:31:19,720 --> 01:31:19,800
What?

1614
01:31:20,030 --> 01:31:21,160
You still wanna do this?

1615
01:31:21,460 --> 01:31:22,140
Why not?

1616
01:31:22,460 --> 01:31:23,660
Are you gonna give up already?

1617
01:31:24,080 --> 01:31:25,080
Uh, alright.

1618
01:31:25,240 --> 01:31:26,240
So what's your plan?

1619
01:31:26,365 --> 01:31:27,940
Let's go for Kakashi himself.

1620
01:31:28,370 --> 01:31:31,720
We'll lure him out to a meal, then
photograph him while he eats.

1621
01:31:31,721 --> 01:31:35,780
We already tried doing that a whole bunch
of times, but nothing we did ever worked.

1622
01:31:36,520 --> 01:31:39,344
Every single time, right at
the very moment when we'd

1623
01:31:39,345 --> 01:31:41,980
have a chance to see his
face, we'd get interrupted.

1624
01:31:42,580 --> 01:31:47,901
Well, with this multi-exposure camera I
built, I bet we can get at least one photo.

1625
01:31:52,280 --> 01:31:52,720
Sensei!

1626
01:31:52,955 --> 01:31:56,320
I need to talk to you about something very
important, you know?

1627
01:31:57,180 --> 01:31:58,180
What is it?

1628
01:31:58,740 --> 01:31:59,180
Uh...

1629
01:31:59,720 --> 01:32:01,700
Actually, why don't we eat some dumplings?

1630
01:32:01,720 --> 01:32:02,720
Dumplings while we talk!

1631
01:32:03,295 --> 01:32:04,980
Okay, I'm ready to go.

1632
01:32:06,280 --> 01:32:07,280
Well, alright.

1633
01:32:08,050 --> 01:32:09,050
Don't mind if I do.

1634
01:32:31,890 --> 01:32:32,990
Oh, hey, Naruto.

1635
01:32:33,680 --> 01:32:35,310
You guys out taking a little break,
too?

1636
01:32:36,970 --> 01:32:38,290
Don't bother us right now!

1637
01:32:38,430 --> 01:32:40,090
We're doing something really important!

1638
01:32:40,390 --> 01:32:41,390
Like what?

1639
01:32:44,870 --> 01:32:47,470
I was just about to find that out.

1640
01:32:47,910 --> 01:32:48,430
What?

1641
01:32:48,690 --> 01:32:49,690
He already ate them?

1642
01:32:51,290 --> 01:32:51,810
Hehehe.

1643
01:32:51,811 --> 01:32:54,390
But this time we got him on camera!

1644
01:33:05,230 --> 01:33:10,960
How can this be?

1645
01:33:11,220 --> 01:33:12,220
It's impossible!

1646
01:33:12,735 --> 01:33:13,800
Are you kidding?

1647
01:33:14,040 --> 01:33:15,040
Not a single one?

1648
01:33:15,420 --> 01:33:18,560
It feels like some divine powers at work
here.

1649
01:33:18,740 --> 01:33:20,080
Yeah, that's a shame.

1650
01:33:20,200 --> 01:33:22,600
Oh well, I guess this means...

1651
01:33:22,750 --> 01:33:27,200
we'll have to say that the mission... is
over and dismissed, huh?

1652
01:33:35,740 --> 01:33:38,980
Alright, I guess it's time
for me to be... Hey, Naruto!

1653
01:33:39,340 --> 01:33:40,340
Hm?

1654
01:33:44,160 --> 01:33:46,700
You want to tell me what's really going on
out here?

1655
01:33:47,340 --> 01:33:48,340
Oh, hey!

1656
01:33:48,380 --> 01:33:49,380
What's up, you guys?

1657
01:34:03,415 --> 01:34:04,800
H-Hikashi-sensei!

1658
01:34:04,801 --> 01:34:05,240
Huh?

1659
01:34:05,241 --> 01:34:06,280
I'm so glad you're here!

1660
01:34:06,695 --> 01:34:11,221
Because, you see, um, it's just that
over there's a... It's going to be alright.

1661
01:34:11,385 --> 01:34:13,600
But first, just calm down and tell me
what's wrong.

1662
01:34:13,860 --> 01:34:17,440
I think that a woman might have drowned
right over there on the riverbank!

1663
01:34:17,840 --> 01:34:18,840
What?

1664
01:34:38,360 --> 01:34:39,940
This is really not good.

1665
01:34:40,060 --> 01:34:41,460
Her pulse is very weak.

1666
01:34:42,020 --> 01:34:42,540
Yes!

1667
01:34:42,900 --> 01:34:44,580
Sakura did an awesome job!

1668
01:34:44,800 --> 01:34:47,560
Her medicines even fooled Takashi-sensei!

1669
01:34:48,820 --> 01:34:50,620
Alright, this calls for it.

1670
01:34:53,740 --> 01:34:54,340
Hehehe!

1671
01:34:54,600 --> 01:34:57,480
He definitely has to take his mask off
now!

1672
01:35:06,300 --> 01:35:07,720
This woman's in danger.

1673
01:35:07,840 --> 01:35:09,080
We can't waste any time.

1674
01:35:09,240 --> 01:35:11,220
We have to get her to the hospital right
away!

1675
01:35:13,420 --> 01:35:18,750
A has failed.

1676
01:35:18,920 --> 01:35:19,520
Understood.

1677
01:35:19,940 --> 01:35:21,760
Everyone switch to Plan B.

1678
01:35:21,761 --> 01:35:23,980
Skaia, please get into position.

1679
01:35:24,745 --> 01:35:25,745
Roger that.

1680
01:35:31,540 --> 01:35:33,050
Okay, he's coming our way now.

1681
01:35:34,210 --> 01:35:37,630
Just as Shikamaru predicted, he's gonna
pass by on his way to the hospital.

1682
01:35:38,180 --> 01:35:39,230
Everyone, get in position.

1683
01:35:44,460 --> 01:35:45,460
Huh?

1684
01:35:47,060 --> 01:35:48,060
Expansion jutsu!

1685
01:35:49,620 --> 01:35:50,740
Human boulder!

1686
01:35:52,920 --> 01:35:56,460
Row, row, row, row, row, row, row,
row, row, row, row!

1687
01:35:56,500 --> 01:35:58,220
Row, row, row, row, row, row, row,
row, row!

1688
01:36:02,020 --> 01:36:04,260
What are you doing?

1689
01:36:04,400 --> 01:36:06,200
I have to get this woman to...

1690
01:36:11,900 --> 01:36:12,820
Go!

1691
01:36:12,821 --> 01:36:14,420
Hidden Jutsu!

1692
01:36:14,421 --> 01:36:15,440
Beetle Spear!

1693
01:36:18,460 --> 01:36:19,460
Now!

1694
01:36:23,430 --> 01:36:26,470
Three, two, one, go!

1695
01:36:27,090 --> 01:36:28,090
Scatter!

1696
01:36:30,410 --> 01:36:31,990
Mine Transfer Jutsu!

1697
01:36:37,030 --> 01:36:38,570
Ribbit, ribbit, ribbit, ribbit!

1698
01:36:43,745 --> 01:36:45,398
Look, you guys, I get
that you want to see

1699
01:36:45,399 --> 01:36:47,670
what I look like, but
we have a situation here.

1700
01:36:47,900 --> 01:36:50,110
She needs to get to the hospital as soon
as...

1701
01:36:57,940 --> 01:37:00,160
Shadow Possession Jutsu, now complete.

1702
01:37:08,340 --> 01:37:09,140
All right!

1703
01:37:09,260 --> 01:37:10,280
Sakeya, do it now!

1704
01:37:14,220 --> 01:37:16,020
It finally worked, Naruto.

1705
01:37:17,020 --> 01:37:19,900
Guess you get to have those ramen and
gyoza now.

1706
01:37:20,960 --> 01:37:21,540
Haha!

1707
01:37:21,780 --> 01:37:23,080
Hey guys, see that?

1708
01:37:23,320 --> 01:37:24,700
The plan actually worked!

1709
01:37:26,080 --> 01:37:27,240
Yeah, finally.

1710
01:37:27,600 --> 01:37:29,520
You should all be grateful to us.

1711
01:37:29,700 --> 01:37:33,800
The reason is because... Okay,
Kagashi-sensei, I hope you're ready!

1712
01:37:34,120 --> 01:37:35,120
Do it, Shikamaru!

1713
01:37:35,360 --> 01:37:37,180
It's time for the unveiling!

1714
01:37:37,695 --> 01:37:39,240
Wait, you guys, hold on!

1715
01:37:39,260 --> 01:37:41,600
Come on, why don't we just talk things
over, okay?

1716
01:37:44,620 --> 01:37:46,040
Hey, hold on a second.

1717
01:37:46,220 --> 01:37:46,700
Stop!

1718
01:37:46,980 --> 01:37:47,980
Just stop!

1719
01:37:50,760 --> 01:37:51,980
Let's all calm down.

1720
01:37:52,280 --> 01:37:57,781
I mean, having this remain as a mystery
makes it much more alluring, don't you think?

1721
01:37:58,400 --> 01:38:01,660
Ramen and Gyoza Ichiraku sound more
alluring to me.

1722
01:38:02,360 --> 01:38:05,380
You mean to tell me all of you were bribed
to do this?

1723
01:38:05,980 --> 01:38:06,940
That's checkmate.

1724
01:38:06,941 --> 01:38:08,560
Alright, now stop!

1725
01:38:08,800 --> 01:38:10,800
I mean, please, you guys, wait!

1726
01:38:20,160 --> 01:38:21,660
You're so annoying, Lee!

1727
01:38:22,500 --> 01:38:23,960
Please, spar with me, Netty!

1728
01:38:25,760 --> 01:38:26,280
What?

1729
01:38:26,460 --> 01:38:27,140
Hey, stop!

1730
01:38:27,280 --> 01:38:28,280
Don't interfere!

1731
01:38:29,270 --> 01:38:30,720
Seriously, come on already!

1732
01:38:30,980 --> 01:38:31,980
Enough is enough!

1733
01:38:41,700 --> 01:38:42,180
Hey!

1734
01:38:42,520 --> 01:38:43,520
Wait for me!

1735
01:38:47,460 --> 01:38:48,460
Sorry!

1736
01:39:05,350 --> 01:39:07,020
He was a shadow clone?

1737
01:39:07,240 --> 01:39:09,000
What the hell is going on here?

1738
01:39:09,390 --> 01:39:12,060
Was Kakashi-sensei onto us right from the
very start?

1739
01:39:22,460 --> 01:39:25,660
Well, it's too bad, but I really am
grateful to all of you.

1740
01:39:26,100 --> 01:39:27,100
No way!

1741
01:39:27,420 --> 01:39:28,940
We all had such an awesome time!

1742
01:39:29,120 --> 01:39:30,880
And it's actually because of you,
Sakeya!

1743
01:39:31,240 --> 01:39:32,280
So, thank you!

1744
01:39:32,640 --> 01:39:34,140
I better get going now.

1745
01:39:35,080 --> 01:39:37,120
Call me anytime if something comes up.

1746
01:39:38,280 --> 01:39:41,080
I really hope you get that scoop that you
wanted!

1747
01:39:52,100 --> 01:39:52,540
Of course!

1748
01:39:52,541 --> 01:39:54,680
It seems like they had a lot of fun...

1749
01:39:56,680 --> 01:39:57,840
If only the two of us stayed!

1750
01:40:04,720 --> 01:40:05,916
I don't know how you can claim that,
but you've been such quite a good friend!

1751
01:40:05,940 --> 01:40:07,396
And I'm actually very impressed by your
friendship!

1752
01:40:07,420 --> 01:40:11,400
It was quite a coincidence that Kiba
happened to show up at the dumpling shop.

1753
01:40:11,640 --> 01:40:14,320
Huh, who would have thought that all of
them would team up?

1754
01:40:14,740 --> 01:40:17,100
I think that something like this is good
for them.

1755
01:40:17,160 --> 01:40:18,380
At least every once in a while.

1756
01:40:18,381 --> 01:40:21,180
Yeah, but I gotta say, this really wore me
out.

1757
01:40:21,660 --> 01:40:24,520
It's tiring to use so many clones and
transformations.

1758
01:40:26,300 --> 01:40:30,440
It was a really close call with my mask
because everyone had such good teamwork.

1759
01:40:31,320 --> 01:40:33,226
Of course, even if they
did get the mask off,

1760
01:40:33,227 --> 01:40:35,961
there wouldn't have
been any real hard done.

1761
01:40:38,120 --> 01:40:40,480
Because I'm wearing a backup mask
underneath.

1762
01:40:42,760 --> 01:40:45,240
I still think food is the best way.

1763
01:40:45,241 --> 01:40:47,620
Yeah, it probably is our best chance.

1764
01:40:47,840 --> 01:40:52,240
But the problem is, how do we get
Kakashi-sensei to eat with us?

1765
01:40:52,660 --> 01:40:53,660
Bad timing!

1766
01:40:53,840 --> 01:40:54,840
Here they come!

1767
01:41:09,020 --> 01:41:10,020
Hey!

1768
01:41:24,450 --> 01:41:25,450
Excuse me.

1769
01:41:25,510 --> 01:41:26,170
Excuse me.

1770
01:41:26,171 --> 01:41:28,270
Did you notice any trouble going on around
here?

1771
01:41:28,490 --> 01:41:28,790
Huh?

1772
01:41:29,340 --> 01:41:31,790
No, I didn't see anything at all.

1773
01:41:43,430 --> 01:41:48,770
Kakashi... I heard that he and his team
were causing a commotion around town.

1774
01:41:49,770 --> 01:41:52,670
Anyway, my apologies for stopping you.

1775
01:41:52,900 --> 01:41:54,010
It's okay.

1776
01:41:58,639 --> 01:41:59,639
Hey!

1777
01:42:09,250 --> 01:42:11,790
Uh, can I, uh, help you with something?

1778
01:42:12,810 --> 01:42:15,410
Don't I know you from somewhere?

1779
01:42:16,290 --> 01:42:17,290
Uh, no.

1780
01:42:17,370 --> 01:42:19,490
I don't think we've ever met before.

1781
01:42:20,270 --> 01:42:20,590
Really?

1782
01:42:21,110 --> 01:42:23,150
Okay then, well, excuse me.

1783
01:42:23,570 --> 01:42:24,570
See you later.

1784
01:42:26,085 --> 01:42:29,390
I could've sworn I met that guy somewhere
before.

1785
01:42:29,850 --> 01:42:31,890
Oh well, I guess it doesn't matter.

1786
01:42:57,585 --> 01:42:58,585
Besides,

1787
01:43:19,940 --> 01:43:20,380
I'm not a fool, you know?

1788
01:43:20,381 --> 01:43:20,520
I think I know what I'm doing.

1789
01:43:20,521 --> 01:43:21,320
This is the last time you'll ever get to
see me.

1790
01:43:21,321 --> 01:43:21,560
Come on, get up and get out of the car.

1791
01:43:21,740 --> 01:43:22,120
You'll be fine.

1792
01:43:22,170 --> 01:43:23,240
Kusui, can I talk to you?

1793
01:43:23,241 --> 01:43:23,340
Of course.

1794
01:43:23,341 --> 01:43:24,341
I'll be fine.

1795
01:43:25,040 --> 01:43:25,780
Okay.

1796
01:43:26,030 --> 01:43:27,030
See you.

1797
01:43:39,260 --> 01:43:42,200
It actually turned out to be a good
mission after all.

1798
01:43:43,080 --> 01:43:45,621
Plus, I have to say, their
teamwork has gotten much

1799
01:43:45,622 --> 01:43:48,021
better than it was during
the bell-snatching mission.

1800
01:43:49,380 --> 01:43:53,160
Well, I'll only be able to do this a
couple more times.

1801
01:45:07,470 --> 01:45:10,410
Don't cry, cause you're so right.

1802
01:45:10,710 --> 01:45:17,290
Don't try with fakes or fears,
cause you will hate yourself in the end.

1803
01:45:17,570 --> 01:45:20,750
Don't try to look so wise.

1804
01:45:20,970 --> 01:45:24,130
Don't cry, cause you're so right.

1805
01:45:24,430 --> 01:45:26,270
Don't try with...

